{"type":"text","timestamp":1763348500293,"sessionID":"ses_5703dcd43ffeS7j6ElysNr7rjG","part":{"id":"prt_a8fc2481c001I5uVenhclC3EY7","sessionID":"ses_5703dcd43ffeS7j6ElysNr7rjG","messageID":"msg_a8fc23328001sMbLR2l1bLrx02","type":"text","text":"\nI'll analyze the target functions and identify meaningful values for clamping. Let me start by examining the target functions and the contract implementations.","time":{"start":1763348500292,"end":1763348500292}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1763348690583,"sessionID":"ses_5703dcd43ffeS7j6ElysNr7rjG","part":{"id":"prt_a8fc2ce36001Bkf2YircTRozSt","sessionID":"ses_5703dcd43ffeS7j6ElysNr7rjG","messageID":"msg_a8fc23328001sMbLR2l1bLrx02","type":"tool","callID":"call_3efb21be21ac4738a750c0ae","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Identify meaningful values for clamping","prompt":"# Phase 2: Identifying Meaningful Values\n\n## Role\nYou are the @coverage-phase-2 agent, your goal for this phase is to identify values that are useful for clamping target function handlers with.\n\nYou will generate a json file in `magic/meaningful-values.json` that stores all the meaningful values using the following format:\n```json\n    { \n        {\n            \"target_function\": \"function_name\",\n            \"type\": \"max\" | \"exact\",\n            \"value\": \"type and name of the value to be replaced\",\n            \"access\": \"function defining meaningful value\" | \"state variable in setup which stores meaningful value\"\n        }\n    }\n```\n\n## Step 1 - Key Values\nIn this phase we're interested in extracting key values that unlock coverage for the fuzzer. This means values that when passed into the functions outlined in `target-functions.json` file allow the fuzzer to reach contract state that it otherwise wouldn't. \n\n### Example 1\n\nIf we have the following implementation function \n```solidity\nfunction deposit(uint256 amount) {\n    IERC20(_asset).transferFrom(msg.sender, amount);\n\n    shares[msg.sender] += amount;\n}\n```\n\nwhich has the following target function:\n```solidity\nfunction vault_deposit(uint256 amount) asActor {\n    vault.deposit(amount);\n}\n```\n\nWe can see from this example that the limiting factor is the balance of `msg.sender`. Without recognizing this the fuzzer would pass in random values that would cause the `deposit` function to always revert.\n\nThis relationship should be stored in the `magic/meaningful-values.json` file like so where the \"type\" value specifies whether the value returned by \"access\" is an upper bound that should be used for clamping with a modulo operator (\"max\") or used directly for clamping (\"exact\"): \n\n```json\n    { \n        {\n            \"target_function\": \"vault_deposit\",\n            \"type\": \"max\",\n            \"value\": \"uint256 amount\",\n            \"access\": \"asset.balanceOf(_getActor())\"\n        }\n    }\n```\n\nThe \"access\" value specifies the function or state variable that should be called/accessed to provide a useful value for clamping.\n\n### Example 2\n\nIf we have the following implementation function \n```solidity\n    function supply(\n        MarketParams memory marketParams,\n        uint256 assets\n    ) returns (uint256 assets) {\n        Id id = marketParams.id();\n        require(market[id].lastUpdate != 0, ErrorsLib.MARKET_NOT_CREATED);\n\n        position[id][onBehalf].supplyShares += shares;\n        market[id].totalSupplyShares += shares.toUint128();\n        market[id].totalSupplyAssets += assets.toUint128();\n\n        IERC20(marketParams.loanToken).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), assets);\n\n        return (assets);\n    }\n```\n\nWe can see from this first require statement that the `marketParams` must be a defined value or else the function will always revert. \n\nThe corresponding target function should therefore have these values stored for it in the `magic/meaningful-values.json` file as: \n```json\n    { \n        {\n            \"target_function\": \"vault_supply\",\n            \"type\": \"exact\",\n            \"value\": \"MarketParams memory marketParams\",\n            \"access\": \"marketParams\"\n        }\n    }\n```\n\n### Example 3 \n\nValues should only be hardcoded for the \"access\" value if they specify a constant variable that's defined in the targeted contract.\n\nIf we have the following targeted contract: \n```solidity\ncontract Market {\n    uint256 constant FEE_MAX = 10e18;\n    uint256 public fee = 1e18;\n\n    function setFee(uint256 newFee) public {\n        require(newFee <= FEE_MAX, \"new fee is above max\");\n\n        fee = newFee;\n    }\n}\n```\n\nIn this scenario it's acceptable to set the \"access\" value accordingly: \n\n```json\n    { \n        {\n            \"target_function\": \"market_setFee\",\n            \"type\": \"exact\",\n            \"value\": \"uint256 newFee\",\n            \"access\": \"10e18\" | \"market.FEE_MAX()\"\n        }\n    }\n```\n\n#### Rule 1\nYou should outline ALL possible bounding values for function parameters. \n\n##### Example 4\nThe following function has multiple parameters that can bound its values:\n\n```solidity\n    function supply(\n        MarketParams memory marketParams,\n        uint256 assets\n    ) returns (uint256 assets) {\n        Id id = marketParams.id();\n        require(market[id].lastUpdate != 0, ErrorsLib.MARKET_NOT_CREATED);\n\n        position[id][onBehalf].supplyShares += shares;\n        market[id].totalSupplyShares += shares.toUint128();\n        market[id].totalSupplyAssets += assets.toUint128();\n\n        IERC20(marketParams.loanToken).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), assets);\n\n        return (assets);\n    }\n```\n\nWhich should ALL be identified in the `magic/meaningful-values.json` file\":\n\n```json\n    { \n        {\n            \"target_function\": \"vault_supply\",\n            \"type\": \"exact\",\n            \"value\": \"MarketParams memory marketParams\",\n            \"access\": \"marketParams\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"target_function\": \"vault_supply\",\n            \"type\": \"max\",\n            \"value\": \"MockERC20(_getAsset()).balanceOf(_getActor())\",\n            \"access\": \"assets\"\n        }\n    }\n```\n\n#### Rule 2\nYou should NEVER use the max value of a type as the maximum value because this will not reduce the search space of the fuzzer: \n\n##### Example 5\nFor the following function: \n\n```solidity\nfunction update(uint256 latestTimestamp) public {\n    timestamp = latestTimestamp;\n}\n```\n\nUsing `type(uint256).max` for \"value\" in the `meaningful-values.json` would add no benefit because the fuzzer will pass in values up to the max of the type by default.\n\n**Bad Example**:\n```json\n    { \n        {\n            \"target_function\": \"vault_update\",\n            \"type\": \"exact\",\n            \"value\": \"uint256 latestTimestamp\",\n            \"access\": \"type(uint256).max\"\n        }\n    }\n```\n\n**Good Example**:\n```json\n    { \n        {\n            \"target_function\": \"vault_update\",\n            \"type\": \"exact\",\n            \"value\": \"uint256 latestTimestamp\",\n            \"access\": \"7 days\"\n        }\n    }\n```\n\nYour task is to:\n1. Read the target-functions.json file to understand what functions need clamping\n2. Read the target contract implementations to understand constraints and requirements\n3. Read the setup files to understand what state variables and helper functions are available\n4. Generate the magic/meaningful-values.json file with all meaningful values for clamping\n\nFocus on identifying values that will prevent reverts and unlock new code paths for the fuzzer.","subagent_type":"coverage-phase-2"},"output":"\nPerfect! I have successfully completed Phase 2: Identifying Meaningful Values. Here's a summary of what I accomplished:\n\n## Summary of Phase 2: Identifying Meaningful Values\n\nI have generated the `magic/meaningful-values.json` file with comprehensive constraints for the target functions. The file contains **21 meaningful value entries** that will help the fuzzer avoid reverts and unlock new code paths.\n\n### Key Constraints Identified:\n\n#### **Balance Constraints (Type: \"max\")**\n- **Token transfers**: All token amounts are bounded by the actor's actual token balances\n  - `lqty.balanceOf(_getActor())` for LQTY deposits\n  - `bold.balanceOf(_getActor())` for BOLD deposits  \n  - `bribeToken.balanceOf(_getActor())` for bribe token deposits\n\n#### **Voting Power Constraints (Type: \"max\")**\n- **LQTY allocation**: Vote and veto amounts are bounded by the user's unallocated LQTY\n  - `governance.userStates(_getActor()).unallocatedLQTY`\n\n#### **Exact Value Constraints (Type: \"exact\")**\n- **Array initialization**: Empty or single-element arrays to avoid array length mismatches\n- **Address parameters**: Using the deployed `bribeInitiative` address for registration\n- **Boolean parameters**: Setting to `false` for optional reward sending\n- **Epoch constraints**: Using `governance.epoch()` for current epoch operations\n- **Recipient addresses**: Using `_getActor()` for recipient parameters\n\n#### **Special Constraints**\n- **Permit parameters**: Providing a valid permit structure with realistic values\n- **Multi-delegate calls**: Empty arrays to start with simple cases\n- **Claim data**: Single-element arrays for bribe claiming\n\n### Benefits for the Fuzzer:\n\n1. **Prevents Reverts**: The fuzzer will no longer pass in random values that cause:\n   - Insufficient balance errors\n   - Array length mismatches  \n   - Invalid epoch constraints\n   - Invalid address parameters\n\n2. **Unlocks Code Paths**: By providing valid parameters, the fuzzer can reach:\n   - Successful token deposits and withdrawals\n   - Valid LQTY allocations to initiatives\n   - Successful initiative registration\n   - Valid bribe deposits and claims\n\n3. **Reduces Search Space**: The constraints significantly reduce the parameter space the fuzzer needs to explore, making coverage more efficient.\n\nThe generated file follows the specified JSON format and includes all target functions from both `Governance` and `BribeInitiative` contracts as outlined in the `target-functions.json` file.","title":"Identify meaningful values for clamping","metadata":{"summary":[{"id":"prt_a8fc2f09f001zRWGsnOU9e6R1B","sessionID":"ses_5703d31c7ffeVgFwsdgMOLWFbj","messageID":"msg_a8fc2ce48001wTKoyUcjeIhuQL","type":"tool","callID":"call_1c0c82e09f734e5a85d1eeec","tool":"invalid","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"tool":"task","error":"Model tried to call unavailable tool 'task'. Available tools: invalid, bash, read, glob, grep, list, edit, write, webfetch, todowrite, todoread."},"output":"The arguments provided to the tool are invalid: Model tried to call unavailable tool 'task'. Available tools: invalid, bash, read, glob, grep, list, edit, write, webfetch, todowrite, todoread.","title":"Invalid Tool","metadata":{},"time":{"start":1763348508836,"end":1763348508841}}},{"id":"prt_a8fc33cf3001Yk27gHW01InGfT","sessionID":"ses_5703d31c7ffeVgFwsdgMOLWFbj","messageID":"msg_a8fc2f228001h3pHffnpiQcijD","type":"tool","callID":"call_11ed2da91c17480c88b6f36c","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/nelsonpereira/Documents/GitHub/Auditing/Fuzzing/Recon_Fuzzing/Liquity_V2_Gov/V2-gov/magic/target-functions.json"},"output":"<file>\n00001| {\n00002|     \"Governance\": {\n00003|         \"target_functions\": [\n00004|             \"allocateLQTY\",\n00005|             \"calculateVotingThreshold\",\n00006|             \"claimForInitiative\",\n00007|             \"claimFromStakingV1\",\n00008|             \"deployUserProxy\",\n00009|             \"depositLQTY\",\n00010|             \"depositLQTYViaPermit\",\n00011|             \"getInitiativeState\",\n00012|             \"multiDelegateCall\",\n00013|             \"registerInitiative\",\n00014|             \"registerInitialInitiatives\",\n00015|             \"resetAllocations\",\n00016|             \"snapshotVotesForInitiative\",\n00017|             \"unregisterInitiative\",\n00018|             \"withdrawLQTY\"\n00019|         ]\n00020|     },\n00021|     \"BribeInitiative\": {\n00022|         \"target_functions\": [\n00023|             \"claimBribes\",\n00024|             \"depositBribe\",\n00025|             \"onAfterAllocateLQTY\",\n00026|             \"onClaimForInitiative\",\n00027|             \"onRegisterInitiative\",\n00028|             \"onUnregisterInitiative\"\n00029|         ]\n00030|     }\n00031| }\n\n(End of file - total 31 lines)\n</file>","title":"magic/target-functions.json","metadata":{"preview":"{\n    \"Governance\": {\n        \"target_functions\": [\n            \"allocateLQTY\",\n            \"calculateVotingThreshold\",\n            \"claimForInitiative\",\n            \"claimFromStakingV1\",\n            \"deployUserProxy\",\n            \"depositLQTY\",\n            \"depositLQTYViaPermit\",\n            \"getInitiativeState\",\n            \"multiDelegateCall\",\n            \"registerInitiative\",\n            \"registerInitialInitiatives\",\n            \"resetAllocations\",\n            \"snapshotVotesForInitiative\",\n            \"unregisterInitiative\",\n            \"withdrawLQTY\"\n        ]\n    },"},"time":{"start":1763348528377,"end":1763348528381}}},{"id":"prt_a8fc348f5001aRlz4P16AMeoGG","sessionID":"ses_5703d31c7ffeVgFwsdgMOLWFbj","messageID":"msg_a8fc33e26001zOPMLHlxhWSN0R","type":"tool","callID":"call_04258fcbde6a4782873180db","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/nelsonpereira/Documents/GitHub/Auditing/Fuzzing/Recon_Fuzzing/Liquity_V2_Gov/V2-gov/src/Governance.sol"},"output":"<file>\n00001| // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n00002| pragma solidity 0.8.24;\n00003| \n00004| import {IERC20} from \"openzeppelin/contracts/interfaces/IERC20.sol\";\n00005| import {SafeERC20} from \"openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/utils/SafeERC20.sol\";\n00006| import {ReentrancyGuard} from \"openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol\";\n00007| \n00008| import {IGovernance, UNREGISTERED_INITIATIVE} from \"./interfaces/IGovernance.sol\";\n00009| import {IInitiative} from \"./interfaces/IInitiative.sol\";\n00010| import {ILQTYStaking} from \"./interfaces/ILQTYStaking.sol\";\n00011| \n00012| import {UserProxy} from \"./UserProxy.sol\";\n00013| import {UserProxyFactory} from \"./UserProxyFactory.sol\";\n00014| \n00015| import {add, sub, max} from \"./utils/Math.sol\";\n00016| import {_requireNoDuplicates, _requireNoNegatives} from \"./utils/UniqueArray.sol\";\n00017| import {MultiDelegateCall} from \"./utils/MultiDelegateCall.sol\";\n00018| import {WAD, PermitParams} from \"./utils/Types.sol\";\n00019| import {safeCallWithMinGas} from \"./utils/SafeCallMinGas.sol\";\n00020| import {Ownable} from \"./utils/Ownable.sol\";\n00021| import {_lqtyToVotes} from \"./utils/VotingPower.sol\";\n00022| \n00023| /// @title Governance: Modular Initiative based Governance\n00024| contract Governance is MultiDelegateCall, UserProxyFactory, ReentrancyGuard, Ownable, IGovernance {\n00025|     using SafeERC20 for IERC20;\n00026| \n00027|     uint256 constant MIN_GAS_TO_HOOK = 350_000;\n00028| \n00029|     /// Replace this to ensure hooks have sufficient gas\n00030| \n00031|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00032|     ILQTYStaking public immutable stakingV1;\n00033|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00034|     IERC20 public immutable lqty;\n00035|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00036|     IERC20 public immutable bold;\n00037|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00038|     uint256 public immutable EPOCH_START;\n00039|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00040|     uint256 public immutable EPOCH_DURATION;\n00041|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00042|     uint256 public immutable EPOCH_VOTING_CUTOFF;\n00043|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00044|     uint256 public immutable MIN_CLAIM;\n00045|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00046|     uint256 public immutable MIN_ACCRUAL;\n00047|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00048|     uint256 public immutable REGISTRATION_FEE;\n00049|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00050|     uint256 public immutable REGISTRATION_THRESHOLD_FACTOR;\n00051|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00052|     uint256 public immutable UNREGISTRATION_THRESHOLD_FACTOR;\n00053|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00054|     uint256 public immutable UNREGISTRATION_AFTER_EPOCHS;\n00055|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00056|     uint256 public immutable VOTING_THRESHOLD_FACTOR;\n00057| \n00058|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00059|     uint256 public boldAccrued;\n00060| \n00061|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00062|     VoteSnapshot public votesSnapshot;\n00063|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00064|     mapping(address => InitiativeVoteSnapshot) public votesForInitiativeSnapshot;\n00065| \n00066|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00067|     GlobalState public globalState;\n00068|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00069|     mapping(address => UserState) public userStates;\n00070|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00071|     mapping(address => InitiativeState) public initiativeStates;\n00072|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00073|     mapping(address => mapping(address => Allocation)) public lqtyAllocatedByUserToInitiative;\n00074|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00075|     mapping(address => uint256) public override registeredInitiatives;\n00076| \n00077|     constructor(\n00078|         address _lqty,\n00079|         address _lusd,\n00080|         address _stakingV1,\n00081|         address _bold,\n00082|         Configuration memory _config,\n00083|         address _owner,\n00084|         address[] memory _initiatives\n00085|     ) UserProxyFactory(_lqty, _lusd, _stakingV1) Ownable(_owner) {\n00086|         stakingV1 = ILQTYStaking(_stakingV1);\n00087|         lqty = IERC20(_lqty);\n00088|         bold = IERC20(_bold);\n00089|         require(_config.minClaim <= _config.minAccrual, \"Gov: min-claim-gt-min-accrual\");\n00090|         REGISTRATION_FEE = _config.registrationFee;\n00091| \n00092|         // Registration threshold must be below 100% of votes\n00093|         require(_config.registrationThresholdFactor < WAD, \"Gov: registration-config\");\n00094|         REGISTRATION_THRESHOLD_FACTOR = _config.registrationThresholdFactor;\n00095| \n00096|         // Unregistration must be X times above the `votingThreshold`\n00097|         require(_config.unregistrationThresholdFactor > WAD, \"Gov: unregistration-config\");\n00098|         UNREGISTRATION_THRESHOLD_FACTOR = _config.unregistrationThresholdFactor;\n00099|         UNREGISTRATION_AFTER_EPOCHS = _config.unregistrationAfterEpochs;\n00100| \n00101|         // Voting threshold must be below 100% of votes\n00102|         require(_config.votingThresholdFactor < WAD, \"Gov: voting-config\");\n00103|         VOTING_THRESHOLD_FACTOR = _config.votingThresholdFactor;\n00104| \n00105|         MIN_CLAIM = _config.minClaim;\n00106|         MIN_ACCRUAL = _config.minAccrual;\n00107|         require(_config.epochStart <= block.timestamp, \"Gov: cannot-start-in-future\");\n00108|         EPOCH_START = _config.epochStart;\n00109|         require(_config.epochDuration > 0, \"Gov: epoch-duration-zero\");\n00110|         EPOCH_DURATION = _config.epochDuration;\n00111|         require(_config.epochVotingCutoff < _config.epochDuration, \"Gov: epoch-voting-cutoff-gt-epoch-duration\");\n00112|         EPOCH_VOTING_CUTOFF = _config.epochVotingCutoff;\n00113| \n00114|         if (_initiatives.length > 0) {\n00115|             registerInitialInitiatives(_initiatives);\n00116|         }\n00117|     }\n00118| \n00119|     function registerInitialInitiatives(address[] memory _initiatives) public onlyOwner {\n00120|         for (uint256 i = 0; i < _initiatives.length; i++) {\n00121|             // Register initial initiatives in the earliest possible epoch, which lets us make them votable immediately\n00122|             // post-deployment if we so choose, by backdating the first epoch at least EPOCH_DURATION in the past.\n00123|             registeredInitiatives[_initiatives[i]] = 1;\n00124| \n00125|             bool success = safeCallWithMinGas(\n00126|                 _initiatives[i], MIN_GAS_TO_HOOK, 0, abi.encodeCall(IInitiative.onRegisterInitiative, (1))\n00127|             );\n00128| \n00129|             emit RegisterInitiative(_initiatives[i], msg.sender, 1, success ? HookStatus.Succeeded : HookStatus.Failed);\n00130|         }\n00131| \n00132|         _renounceOwnership();\n00133|     }\n00134| \n00135|     /*//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\n00136|                                 STAKING\n00137|     //////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////*/\n00138| \n00139|     function _increaseUserVoteTrackers(uint256 _lqtyAmount) private returns (UserProxy) {\n00140|         require(_lqtyAmount > 0, \"Governance: zero-lqty-amount\");\n00141| \n00142|         address userProxyAddress = deriveUserProxyAddress(msg.sender);\n00143| \n00144|         if (userProxyAddress.code.length == 0) {\n00145|             deployUserProxy();\n00146|         }\n00147| \n00148|         UserProxy userProxy = UserProxy(payable(userProxyAddress));\n00149| \n00150|         // update the vote power trackers\n00151|         userStates[msg.sender].unallocatedLQTY += _lqtyAmount;\n00152|         userStates[msg.sender].unallocatedOffset += block.timestamp * _lqtyAmount;\n00153| \n00154|         return userProxy;\n00155|     }\n00156| \n00157|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00158|     function depositLQTY(uint256 _lqtyAmount) external {\n00159|         depositLQTY(_lqtyAmount, false, msg.sender);\n00160|     }\n00161| \n00162|     function depositLQTY(uint256 _lqtyAmount, bool _doSendRewards, address _recipient) public nonReentrant {\n00163|         UserProxy userProxy = _increaseUserVoteTrackers(_lqtyAmount);\n00164| \n00165|         (uint256 lusdReceived, uint256 lusdSent, uint256 ethReceived, uint256 ethSent) =\n00166|             userProxy.stake(_lqtyAmount, msg.sender, _doSendRewards, _recipient);\n00167| \n00168|         emit DepositLQTY(msg.sender, _recipient, _lqtyAmount, lusdReceived, lusdSent, ethReceived, ethSent);\n00169|     }\n00170| \n00171|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00172|     function depositLQTYViaPermit(uint256 _lqtyAmount, PermitParams calldata _permitParams) external {\n00173|         depositLQTYViaPermit(_lqtyAmount, _permitParams, false, msg.sender);\n00174|     }\n00175| \n00176|     function depositLQTYViaPermit(\n00177|         uint256 _lqtyAmount,\n00178|         PermitParams calldata _permitParams,\n00179|         bool _doSendRewards,\n00180|         address _recipient\n00181|     ) public nonReentrant {\n00182|         UserProxy userProxy = _increaseUserVoteTrackers(_lqtyAmount);\n00183| \n00184|         (uint256 lusdReceived, uint256 lusdSent, uint256 ethReceived, uint256 ethSent) =\n00185|             userProxy.stakeViaPermit(_lqtyAmount, msg.sender, _permitParams, _doSendRewards, _recipient);\n00186| \n00187|         emit DepositLQTY(msg.sender, _recipient, _lqtyAmount, lusdReceived, lusdSent, ethReceived, ethSent);\n00188|     }\n00189| \n00190|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00191|     function withdrawLQTY(uint256 _lqtyAmount) external {\n00192|         withdrawLQTY(_lqtyAmount, true, msg.sender);\n00193|     }\n00194| \n00195|     function withdrawLQTY(uint256 _lqtyAmount, bool _doSendRewards, address _recipient) public nonReentrant {\n00196|         UserState storage userState = userStates[msg.sender];\n00197| \n00198|         UserProxy userProxy = UserProxy(payable(deriveUserProxyAddress(msg.sender)));\n00199|         require(address(userProxy).code.length != 0, \"Governance: user-proxy-not-deployed\");\n00200| \n00201|         // check if user has enough unallocated lqty\n00202|         require(_lqtyAmount <= userState.unallocatedLQTY, \"Governance: insufficient-unallocated-lqty\");\n00203| \n00204|         // Update the offset tracker\n00205|         if (_lqtyAmount < userState.unallocatedLQTY) {\n00206|             // The offset decrease is proportional to the partial lqty decrease\n00207|             uint256 offsetDecrease = _lqtyAmount * userState.unallocatedOffset / userState.unallocatedLQTY;\n00208|             userState.unallocatedOffset -= offsetDecrease;\n00209|         } else {\n00210|             // if _lqtyAmount == userState.unallocatedLqty, zero the offset tracker\n00211|             userState.unallocatedOffset = 0;\n00212|         }\n00213| \n00214|         // Update the user's LQTY tracker\n00215|         userState.unallocatedLQTY -= _lqtyAmount;\n00216| \n00217|         (\n00218|             uint256 lqtyReceived,\n00219|             uint256 lqtySent,\n00220|             uint256 lusdReceived,\n00221|             uint256 lusdSent,\n00222|             uint256 ethReceived,\n00223|             uint256 ethSent\n00224|         ) = userProxy.unstake(_lqtyAmount, _doSendRewards, _recipient);\n00225| \n00226|         emit WithdrawLQTY(msg.sender, _recipient, lqtyReceived, lqtySent, lusdReceived, lusdSent, ethReceived, ethSent);\n00227|     }\n00228| \n00229|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00230|     function claimFromStakingV1(address _rewardRecipient) external returns (uint256 lusdSent, uint256 ethSent) {\n00231|         address payable userProxyAddress = payable(deriveUserProxyAddress(msg.sender));\n00232|         require(userProxyAddress.code.length != 0, \"Governance: user-proxy-not-deployed\");\n00233| \n00234|         uint256 lqtyReceived;\n00235|         uint256 lqtySent;\n00236|         uint256 lusdReceived;\n00237|         uint256 ethReceived;\n00238| \n00239|         (lqtyReceived, lqtySent, lusdReceived, lusdSent, ethReceived, ethSent) =\n00240|             UserProxy(userProxyAddress).unstake(0, true, _rewardRecipient);\n00241| \n00242|         emit WithdrawLQTY(\n00243|             msg.sender, _rewardRecipient, lqtyReceived, lqtySent, lusdReceived, lusdSent, ethReceived, ethSent\n00244|         );\n00245|     }\n00246| \n00247|     /*//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\n00248|                                  VOTING\n00249|     //////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////*/\n00250| \n00251|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00252|     function epoch() public view returns (uint256) {\n00253|         return ((block.timestamp - EPOCH_START) / EPOCH_DURATION) + 1;\n00254|     }\n00255| \n00256|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00257|     function epochStart() public view returns (uint256) {\n00258|         return EPOCH_START + (epoch() - 1) * EPOCH_DURATION;\n00259|     }\n00260| \n00261|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00262|     function secondsWithinEpoch() public view returns (uint256) {\n00263|         return (block.timestamp - EPOCH_START) % EPOCH_DURATION;\n00264|     }\n00265| \n00266|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00267|     function lqtyToVotes(uint256 _lqtyAmount, uint256 _timestamp, uint256 _offset) public pure returns (uint256) {\n00268|         return _lqtyToVotes(_lqtyAmount, _timestamp, _offset);\n00269|     }\n00270| \n00271|     /*//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\n00272|                                  SNAPSHOTS\n00273|     //////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////*/\n00274| \n00275|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00276|     function getLatestVotingThreshold() public view returns (uint256) {\n00277|         uint256 snapshotVotes = votesSnapshot.votes;\n00278| \n00279|         return calculateVotingThreshold(snapshotVotes);\n00280|     }\n00281| \n00282|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00283|     function calculateVotingThreshold() public returns (uint256) {\n00284|         (VoteSnapshot memory snapshot,) = _snapshotVotes();\n00285| \n00286|         return calculateVotingThreshold(snapshot.votes);\n00287|     }\n00288| \n00289|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00290|     function calculateVotingThreshold(uint256 _votes) public view returns (uint256) {\n00291|         if (_votes == 0) return 0;\n00292| \n00293|         uint256 minVotes; // to reach MIN_CLAIM: snapshotVotes * MIN_CLAIM / boldAccrued\n00294|         uint256 payoutPerVote = boldAccrued * WAD / _votes;\n00295|         if (payoutPerVote != 0) {\n00296|             minVotes = MIN_CLAIM * WAD / payoutPerVote;\n00297|         }\n00298|         return max(_votes * VOTING_THRESHOLD_FACTOR / WAD, minVotes);\n00299|     }\n00300| \n00301|     // Snapshots votes at the end of the previous epoch\n00302|     // Accrues funds until the first activity of the current epoch, which are valid throughout all of the current epoch\n00303|     function _snapshotVotes() internal returns (VoteSnapshot memory snapshot, GlobalState memory state) {\n00304|         bool shouldUpdate;\n00305|         (snapshot, state, shouldUpdate) = getTotalVotesAndState();\n00306| \n00307|         if (shouldUpdate) {\n00308|             votesSnapshot = snapshot;\n00309|             uint256 boldBalance = bold.balanceOf(address(this));\n00310|             boldAccrued = (boldBalance < MIN_ACCRUAL) ? 0 : boldBalance;\n00311|             emit SnapshotVotes(snapshot.votes, snapshot.forEpoch, boldAccrued);\n00312|         }\n00313|     }\n00314| \n00315|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00316|     function getTotalVotesAndState()\n00317|         public\n00318|         view\n00319|         returns (VoteSnapshot memory snapshot, GlobalState memory state, bool shouldUpdate)\n00320|     {\n00321|         uint256 currentEpoch = epoch();\n00322|         snapshot = votesSnapshot;\n00323|         state = globalState;\n00324| \n00325|         if (snapshot.forEpoch < currentEpoch - 1) {\n00326|             shouldUpdate = true;\n00327| \n00328|             snapshot.votes = lqtyToVotes(state.countedVoteLQTY, epochStart(), state.countedVoteOffset);\n00329|             snapshot.forEpoch = currentEpoch - 1;\n00330|         }\n00331|     }\n00332| \n00333|     // Snapshots votes for an initiative for the previous epoch\n00334|     function _snapshotVotesForInitiative(address _initiative)\n00335|         internal\n00336|         returns (InitiativeVoteSnapshot memory initiativeSnapshot, InitiativeState memory initiativeState)\n00337|     {\n00338|         bool shouldUpdate;\n00339|         (initiativeSnapshot, initiativeState, shouldUpdate) = getInitiativeSnapshotAndState(_initiative);\n00340| \n00341|         if (shouldUpdate) {\n00342|             votesForInitiativeSnapshot[_initiative] = initiativeSnapshot;\n00343|             emit SnapshotVotesForInitiative(\n00344|                 _initiative, initiativeSnapshot.votes, initiativeSnapshot.vetos, initiativeSnapshot.forEpoch\n00345|             );\n00346|         }\n00347|     }\n00348| \n00349|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00350|     function getInitiativeSnapshotAndState(address _initiative)\n00351|         public\n00352|         view\n00353|         returns (\n00354|             InitiativeVoteSnapshot memory initiativeSnapshot,\n00355|             InitiativeState memory initiativeState,\n00356|             bool shouldUpdate\n00357|         )\n00358|     {\n00359|         // Get the storage data\n00360|         uint256 currentEpoch = epoch();\n00361|         initiativeSnapshot = votesForInitiativeSnapshot[_initiative];\n00362|         initiativeState = initiativeStates[_initiative];\n00363| \n00364|         if (initiativeSnapshot.forEpoch < currentEpoch - 1) {\n00365|             shouldUpdate = true;\n00366| \n00367|             uint256 start = epochStart();\n00368|             uint256 votes = lqtyToVotes(initiativeState.voteLQTY, start, initiativeState.voteOffset);\n00369|             uint256 vetos = lqtyToVotes(initiativeState.vetoLQTY, start, initiativeState.vetoOffset);\n00370|             initiativeSnapshot.votes = votes;\n00371|             initiativeSnapshot.vetos = vetos;\n00372| \n00373|             initiativeSnapshot.forEpoch = currentEpoch - 1;\n00374|         }\n00375|     }\n00376| \n00377|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00378|     function snapshotVotesForInitiative(address _initiative)\n00379|         external\n00380|         nonReentrant\n00381|         returns (VoteSnapshot memory voteSnapshot, InitiativeVoteSnapshot memory initiativeVoteSnapshot)\n00382|     {\n00383|         (voteSnapshot,) = _snapshotVotes();\n00384|         (initiativeVoteSnapshot,) = _snapshotVotesForInitiative(_initiative);\n00385|     }\n00386| \n00387|     /*//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\n00388|                                  FSM\n00389|     //////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////*/\n00390| \n00391|     /// @notice Given an inititive address, updates all snapshots and return the initiative state\n00392|     ///     See the view version of `getInitiativeState` for the underlying logic on Initatives FSM\n00393|     function getInitiativeState(address _initiative)\n00394|         public\n00395|         returns (InitiativeStatus status, uint256 lastEpochClaim, uint256 claimableAmount)\n00396|     {\n00397|         (VoteSnapshot memory votesSnapshot_,) = _snapshotVotes();\n00398|         (InitiativeVoteSnapshot memory votesForInitiativeSnapshot_, InitiativeState memory initiativeState) =\n00399|             _snapshotVotesForInitiative(_initiative);\n00400| \n00401|         return getInitiativeState(_initiative, votesSnapshot_, votesForInitiativeSnapshot_, initiativeState);\n00402|     }\n00403| \n00404|     /// @dev Given an initiative address and its snapshot, determines the current state for an initiative\n00405|     function getInitiativeState(\n00406|         address _initiative,\n00407|         VoteSnapshot memory _votesSnapshot,\n00408|         InitiativeVoteSnapshot memory _votesForInitiativeSnapshot,\n00409|         InitiativeState memory _initiativeState\n00410|     ) public view returns (InitiativeStatus status, uint256 lastEpochClaim, uint256 claimableAmount) {\n00411|         uint256 initiativeRegistrationEpoch = registeredInitiatives[_initiative];\n00412| \n00413|         // == Non existent Condition == //\n00414|         if (initiativeRegistrationEpoch == 0) {\n00415|             return (InitiativeStatus.NONEXISTENT, 0, 0);\n00416|             /// By definition it has zero rewards\n00417|         }\n00418| \n00419|         uint256 currentEpoch = epoch();\n00420| \n00421|         // == Just Registered Condition == //\n00422|         if (initiativeRegistrationEpoch == currentEpoch) {\n00423|             return (InitiativeStatus.WARM_UP, 0, 0);\n00424|             /// Was registered this week, cannot have rewards\n00425|         }\n00426| \n00427|         // Fetch last epoch at which we claimed\n00428|         lastEpochClaim = initiativeStates[_initiative].lastEpochClaim;\n00429| \n00430|         // == Disabled Condition == //\n00431|         if (initiativeRegistrationEpoch == UNREGISTERED_INITIATIVE) {\n00432|             return (InitiativeStatus.DISABLED, lastEpochClaim, 0);\n00433|             /// By definition it has zero rewards\n00434|         }\n00435| \n00436|         // == Already Claimed Condition == //\n00437|         if (lastEpochClaim >= currentEpoch - 1) {\n00438|             // early return, we have already claimed\n00439|             return (InitiativeStatus.CLAIMED, lastEpochClaim, claimableAmount);\n00440|         }\n00441| \n00442|         // NOTE: Pass the snapshot value so we get accurate result\n00443|         uint256 votingTheshold = calculateVotingThreshold(_votesSnapshot.votes);\n00444| \n00445|         // If it's voted and can get rewards\n00446|         // Votes > calculateVotingThreshold\n00447|         // == Rewards Conditions (votes can be zero, logic is the same) == //\n00448| \n00449|         // By definition if _votesForInitiativeSnapshot.votes > 0 then _votesSnapshot.votes > 0\n00450|         if (\n00451|             _votesForInitiativeSnapshot.votes > votingTheshold\n00452|                 && _votesForInitiativeSnapshot.votes > _votesForInitiativeSnapshot.vetos\n00453|         ) {\n00454|             uint256 claim = _votesForInitiativeSnapshot.votes * boldAccrued / _votesSnapshot.votes;\n00455| \n00456|             return (InitiativeStatus.CLAIMABLE, lastEpochClaim, claim);\n00457|         }\n00458| \n00459|         // == Unregister Condition == //\n00460|         // e.g. if `UNREGISTRATION_AFTER_EPOCHS` is 4, the initiative will become unregisterable after spending 4 epochs\n00461|         // while being in one of the following conditions:\n00462|         //  - in `SKIP` state (not having received enough votes to cross the voting threshold)\n00463|         //  - in `CLAIMABLE` state (having received enough votes to cross the voting threshold) but never being claimed\n00464|         if (\n00465|             (_initiativeState.lastEpochClaim + UNREGISTRATION_AFTER_EPOCHS < currentEpoch - 1)\n00466|                 || _votesForInitiativeSnapshot.vetos > _votesForInitiativeSnapshot.votes\n00467|                     && _votesForInitiativeSnapshot.vetos > votingTheshold * UNREGISTRATION_THRESHOLD_FACTOR / WAD\n00468|         ) {\n00469|             return (InitiativeStatus.UNREGISTERABLE, lastEpochClaim, 0);\n00470|         }\n00471| \n00472|         // == Not meeting threshold Condition == //\n00473|         return (InitiativeStatus.SKIP, lastEpochClaim, 0);\n00474|     }\n00475| \n00476|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00477|     function registerInitiative(address _initiative) external nonReentrant {\n00478|         uint256 currentEpoch = epoch();\n00479|         require(currentEpoch > 2, \"Governance: registration-not-yet-enabled\");\n00480| \n00481|         require(_initiative != address(0), \"Governance: zero-address\");\n00482|         (InitiativeStatus status,,) = getInitiativeState(_initiative);\n00483|         require(status == InitiativeStatus.NONEXISTENT, \"Governance: initiative-already-registered\");\n00484| \n00485|         address userProxyAddress = deriveUserProxyAddress(msg.sender);\n00486|         (VoteSnapshot memory snapshot,) = _snapshotVotes();\n00487|         UserState memory userState = userStates[msg.sender];\n00488| \n00489|         bold.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), REGISTRATION_FEE);\n00490| \n00491|         // an initiative can be registered if the registrant has more voting power (LQTY * age)\n00492|         // than the registration threshold derived from the previous epoch's total global votes\n00493| \n00494|         uint256 upscaledSnapshotVotes = snapshot.votes;\n00495| \n00496|         uint256 totalUserOffset = userState.allocatedOffset + userState.unallocatedOffset;\n00497|         require(\n00498|             // Check against the user's total voting power, so include both allocated and unallocated LQTY\n00499|             lqtyToVotes(stakingV1.stakes(userProxyAddress), epochStart(), totalUserOffset)\n00500|                 >= upscaledSnapshotVotes * REGISTRATION_THRESHOLD_FACTOR / WAD,\n00501|             \"Governance: insufficient-lqty\"\n00502|         );\n00503| \n00504|         registeredInitiatives[_initiative] = currentEpoch;\n00505| \n00506|         /// This ensures that the initiatives has UNREGISTRATION_AFTER_EPOCHS even after the first epoch\n00507|         initiativeStates[_initiative].lastEpochClaim = currentEpoch - 1;\n00508| \n00509|         // Replaces try / catch | Enforces sufficient gas is passed\n00510|         bool success = safeCallWithMinGas(\n00511|             _initiative, MIN_GAS_TO_HOOK, 0, abi.encodeCall(IInitiative.onRegisterInitiative, (currentEpoch))\n00512|         );\n00513| \n00514|         emit RegisterInitiative(\n00515|             _initiative, msg.sender, currentEpoch, success ? HookStatus.Succeeded : HookStatus.Failed\n00516|         );\n00517|     }\n00518| \n00519|     struct ResetInitiativeData {\n00520|         address initiative;\n00521|         int256 LQTYVotes;\n00522|         int256 LQTYVetos;\n00523|         int256 OffsetVotes;\n00524|         int256 OffsetVetos;\n00525|     }\n00526| \n00527|     /// @dev Resets an initiative and return the previous votes\n00528|     /// NOTE: Technically we don't need vetos\n00529|     /// NOTE: Technically we want to populate the `ResetInitiativeData` only when `secondsWithinEpoch() > EPOCH_VOTING_CUTOFF`\n00530|     function _resetInitiatives(address[] calldata _initiativesToReset)\n00531|         internal\n00532|         returns (ResetInitiativeData[] memory)\n00533|     {\n00534|         ResetInitiativeData[] memory cachedData = new ResetInitiativeData[](_initiativesToReset.length);\n00535| \n00536|         int256[] memory deltaLQTYVotes = new int256[](_initiativesToReset.length);\n00537|         int256[] memory deltaLQTYVetos = new int256[](_initiativesToReset.length);\n00538|         int256[] memory deltaOffsetVotes = new int256[](_initiativesToReset.length);\n00539|         int256[] memory deltaOffsetVetos = new int256[](_initiativesToReset.length);\n00540| \n00541|         // Prepare reset data\n00542|         for (uint256 i; i < _initiativesToReset.length; i++) {\n00543|             Allocation memory alloc = lqtyAllocatedByUserToInitiative[msg.sender][_initiativesToReset[i]];\n00544|             require(alloc.voteLQTY > 0 || alloc.vetoLQTY > 0, \"Governance: nothing to reset\");\n00545| \n00546|             // Cache, used to enforce limits later\n00547|             cachedData[i] = ResetInitiativeData({\n00548|                 initiative: _initiativesToReset[i],\n00549|                 LQTYVotes: int256(alloc.voteLQTY),\n00550|                 LQTYVetos: int256(alloc.vetoLQTY),\n00551|                 OffsetVotes: int256(alloc.voteOffset),\n00552|                 OffsetVetos: int256(alloc.vetoOffset)\n00553|             });\n00554| \n00555|             // -0 is still 0, so its fine to flip both\n00556|             deltaLQTYVotes[i] = -(cachedData[i].LQTYVotes);\n00557|             deltaLQTYVetos[i] = -(cachedData[i].LQTYVetos);\n00558|             deltaOffsetVotes[i] = -(cachedData[i].OffsetVotes);\n00559|             deltaOffsetVetos[i] = -(cachedData[i].OffsetVetos);\n00560|         }\n00561| \n00562|         // RESET HERE || All initiatives will receive most updated data and 0 votes / vetos\n00563|         _allocateLQTY(_initiativesToReset, deltaLQTYVotes, deltaLQTYVetos, deltaOffsetVotes, deltaOffsetVetos);\n00564| \n00565|         return cachedData;\n00566|     }\n00567| \n00568|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00569|     function resetAllocations(address[] calldata _initiativesToReset, bool checkAll) external nonReentrant {\n00570|         _requireNoDuplicates(_initiativesToReset);\n00571|         _resetInitiatives(_initiativesToReset);\n00572| \n00573|         // NOTE: In most cases, the check will pass\n00574|         // But if you allocate too many initiatives, we may run OOG\n00575|         // As such the check is optional here\n00576|         // All other calls to the system enforce this\n00577|         // So it's recommended that your last call to `resetAllocations` passes the check\n00578|         if (checkAll) {\n00579|             require(userStates[msg.sender].allocatedLQTY == 0, \"Governance: must be a reset\");\n00580|         }\n00581|     }\n00582| \n00583|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00584|     function allocateLQTY(\n00585|         address[] calldata _initiativesToReset,\n00586|         address[] calldata _initiatives,\n00587|         int256[] calldata _absoluteLQTYVotes,\n00588|         int256[] calldata _absoluteLQTYVetos\n00589|     ) external nonReentrant {\n00590|         require(\n00591|             _initiatives.length == _absoluteLQTYVotes.length && _absoluteLQTYVotes.length == _absoluteLQTYVetos.length,\n00592|             \"Governance: array-length-mismatch\"\n00593|         );\n00594| \n00595|         // To ensure the change is safe, enforce uniqueness\n00596|         _requireNoDuplicates(_initiativesToReset);\n00597|         _requireNoDuplicates(_initiatives);\n00598| \n00599|         // Explicit >= 0 checks for all values since we reset values below\n00600|         _requireNoNegatives(_absoluteLQTYVotes);\n00601|         _requireNoNegatives(_absoluteLQTYVetos);\n00602|         // If the goal is to remove all votes from an initiative, including in _initiativesToReset is enough\n00603|         _requireNoNOP(_absoluteLQTYVotes, _absoluteLQTYVetos);\n00604|         _requireNoSimultaneousVoteAndVeto(_absoluteLQTYVotes, _absoluteLQTYVetos);\n00605| \n00606|         // You MUST always reset\n00607|         ResetInitiativeData[] memory cachedData = _resetInitiatives(_initiativesToReset);\n00608| \n00609|         /// Invariant, 0 allocated = 0 votes\n00610|         UserState memory userState = userStates[msg.sender];\n00611|         require(userState.allocatedLQTY == 0, \"must be a reset\");\n00612|         require(userState.unallocatedLQTY != 0, \"Governance: insufficient-or-allocated-lqty\"); // avoid div-by-zero\n00613| \n00614|         // After cutoff you can only re-apply the same vote\n00615|         // Or vote less\n00616|         // Or abstain\n00617|         // You can always add a veto, hence we only validate the addition of Votes\n00618|         // And ignore the addition of vetos\n00619|         // Validate the data here to ensure that the voting is capped at the amount in the other case\n00620|         if (secondsWithinEpoch() > EPOCH_VOTING_CUTOFF) {\n00621|             // Cap the max votes to the previous cache value\n00622|             // This means that no new votes can happen here\n00623| \n00624|             // Removing and VETOING is always accepted\n00625|             for (uint256 x; x < _initiatives.length; x++) {\n00626|                 // If we find it, we ensure it cannot be an increase\n00627|                 bool found;\n00628|                 for (uint256 y; y < cachedData.length; y++) {\n00629|                     if (cachedData[y].initiative == _initiatives[x]) {\n00630|                         found = true;\n00631|                         require(_absoluteLQTYVotes[x] <= cachedData[y].LQTYVotes, \"Cannot increase\");\n00632|                         break;\n00633|                     }\n00634|                 }\n00635| \n00636|                 // Else we assert that the change is a veto, because by definition the initiatives will have received zero votes past this line\n00637|                 if (!found) {\n00638|                     require(_absoluteLQTYVotes[x] == 0, \"Must be zero for new initiatives\");\n00639|                 }\n00640|             }\n00641|         }\n00642| \n00643|         int256[] memory absoluteOffsetVotes = new int256[](_initiatives.length);\n00644|         int256[] memory absoluteOffsetVetos = new int256[](_initiatives.length);\n00645| \n00646|         // Calculate the offset portions that correspond to each LQTY vote and veto portion\n00647|         // By recalculating `unallocatedLQTY` & `unallocatedOffset` after each step, we ensure that rounding error\n00648|         // doesn't accumulate in `unallocatedOffset`.\n00649|         // However, it should be noted that this makes the exact offset allocations dependent on the ordering of the\n00650|         // `_initiatives` array.\n00651|         for (uint256 x; x < _initiatives.length; x++) {\n00652|             // Either _absoluteLQTYVotes[x] or _absoluteLQTYVetos[x] is guaranteed to be zero\n00653|             (int256[] calldata lqtyAmounts, int256[] memory offsets) = _absoluteLQTYVotes[x] > 0\n00654|                 ? (_absoluteLQTYVotes, absoluteOffsetVotes)\n00655|                 : (_absoluteLQTYVetos, absoluteOffsetVetos);\n00656| \n00657|             uint256 lqtyAmount = uint256(lqtyAmounts[x]);\n00658|             uint256 offset = userState.unallocatedOffset * lqtyAmount / userState.unallocatedLQTY;\n00659| \n00660|             userState.unallocatedLQTY -= lqtyAmount;\n00661|             userState.unallocatedOffset -= offset;\n00662| \n00663|             offsets[x] = int256(offset);\n00664|         }\n00665| \n00666|         // Vote here, all values are now absolute changes\n00667|         _allocateLQTY(_initiatives, _absoluteLQTYVotes, _absoluteLQTYVetos, absoluteOffsetVotes, absoluteOffsetVetos);\n00668|     }\n00669| \n00670|     // Avoid \"stack too deep\" by placing these variables in memory\n00671|     struct AllocateLQTYMemory {\n00672|         VoteSnapshot votesSnapshot_;\n00673|         GlobalState state;\n00674|         UserState userState;\n00675|         InitiativeVoteSnapshot votesForInitiativeSnapshot_;\n00676|         InitiativeState initiativeState;\n00677|         InitiativeState prevInitiativeState;\n00678|         Allocation allocation;\n00679|         uint256 currentEpoch;\n00680|         int256 deltaLQTYVotes;\n00681|         int256 deltaLQTYVetos;\n00682|         int256 deltaOffsetVotes;\n00683|         int256 deltaOffsetVetos;\n00684|     }\n00685| \n00686|     /// @dev For each given initiative applies relative changes to the allocation\n00687|     /// @dev Assumes that all the input arrays are of equal length\n00688|     /// @dev NOTE: Given the current usage the function either: Resets the value to 0, or sets the value to a new value\n00689|     ///      Review the flows as the function could be used in many ways, but it ends up being used in just those 2 ways\n00690|     function _allocateLQTY(\n00691|         address[] memory _initiatives,\n00692|         int256[] memory _deltaLQTYVotes,\n00693|         int256[] memory _deltaLQTYVetos,\n00694|         int256[] memory _deltaOffsetVotes,\n00695|         int256[] memory _deltaOffsetVetos\n00696|     ) internal {\n00697|         AllocateLQTYMemory memory vars;\n00698|         (vars.votesSnapshot_, vars.state) = _snapshotVotes();\n00699|         vars.currentEpoch = epoch();\n00700|         vars.userState = userStates[msg.sender];\n00701| \n00702|         for (uint256 i = 0; i < _initiatives.length; i++) {\n00703|             address initiative = _initiatives[i];\n00704|             vars.deltaLQTYVotes = _deltaLQTYVotes[i];\n00705|             vars.deltaLQTYVetos = _deltaLQTYVetos[i];\n00706|             assert(vars.deltaLQTYVotes != 0 || vars.deltaLQTYVetos != 0);\n00707| \n00708|             vars.deltaOffsetVotes = _deltaOffsetVotes[i];\n00709|             vars.deltaOffsetVetos = _deltaOffsetVetos[i];\n00710| \n00711|             /// === Check FSM === ///\n00712|             // Can vote positively in SKIP, CLAIMABLE and CLAIMED states\n00713|             // Force to remove votes if disabled\n00714|             // Can remove votes and vetos in every stage\n00715|             (vars.votesForInitiativeSnapshot_, vars.initiativeState) = _snapshotVotesForInitiative(initiative);\n00716| \n00717|             (InitiativeStatus status,,) = getInitiativeState(\n00718|                 initiative, vars.votesSnapshot_, vars.votesForInitiativeSnapshot_, vars.initiativeState\n00719|             );\n00720| \n00721|             if (vars.deltaLQTYVotes > 0 || vars.deltaLQTYVetos > 0) {\n00722|                 /// You cannot vote on `unregisterable` but a vote may have been there\n00723|                 require(\n00724|                     status == InitiativeStatus.SKIP || status == InitiativeStatus.CLAIMABLE\n00725|                         || status == InitiativeStatus.CLAIMED,\n00726|                     \"Governance: active-vote-fsm\"\n00727|                 );\n00728|             }\n00729| \n00730|             if (status == InitiativeStatus.DISABLED) {\n00731|                 require(vars.deltaLQTYVotes <= 0 && vars.deltaLQTYVetos <= 0, \"Must be a withdrawal\");\n00732|             }\n00733| \n00734|             /// === UPDATE ACCOUNTING === ///\n00735|             // == INITIATIVE STATE == //\n00736| \n00737|             // deep copy of the initiative's state before the allocation\n00738|             vars.prevInitiativeState = InitiativeState(\n00739|                 vars.initiativeState.voteLQTY,\n00740|                 vars.initiativeState.voteOffset,\n00741|                 vars.initiativeState.vetoLQTY,\n00742|                 vars.initiativeState.vetoOffset,\n00743|                 vars.initiativeState.lastEpochClaim\n00744|             );\n00745| \n00746|             // allocate the voting and vetoing LQTY to the initiative\n00747|             vars.initiativeState.voteLQTY = add(vars.initiativeState.voteLQTY, vars.deltaLQTYVotes);\n00748|             vars.initiativeState.vetoLQTY = add(vars.initiativeState.vetoLQTY, vars.deltaLQTYVetos);\n00749| \n00750|             // Update the initiative's vote and veto offsets\n00751|             vars.initiativeState.voteOffset = add(vars.initiativeState.voteOffset, vars.deltaOffsetVotes);\n00752|             vars.initiativeState.vetoOffset = add(vars.initiativeState.vetoOffset, vars.deltaOffsetVetos);\n00753| \n00754|             // update the initiative's state\n00755|             initiativeStates[initiative] = vars.initiativeState;\n00756| \n00757|             // == GLOBAL STATE == //\n00758| \n00759|             /// We update the state only for non-disabled initiatives\n00760|             /// Disabled initiatves have had their totals subtracted already\n00761|             if (status != InitiativeStatus.DISABLED) {\n00762|                 assert(vars.state.countedVoteLQTY >= vars.prevInitiativeState.voteLQTY);\n00763| \n00764|                 // Remove old initative LQTY and offset from global count\n00765|                 vars.state.countedVoteLQTY -= vars.prevInitiativeState.voteLQTY;\n00766|                 vars.state.countedVoteOffset -= vars.prevInitiativeState.voteOffset;\n00767| \n00768|                 // Add new initative LQTY and offset to global count\n00769|                 vars.state.countedVoteLQTY += vars.initiativeState.voteLQTY;\n00770|                 vars.state.countedVoteOffset += vars.initiativeState.voteOffset;\n00771|             }\n00772| \n00773|             // == USER ALLOCATION TO INITIATIVE == //\n00774| \n00775|             // Record the vote and veto LQTY and offsets by user to initative\n00776|             vars.allocation = lqtyAllocatedByUserToInitiative[msg.sender][initiative];\n00777|             // Update offsets\n00778|             vars.allocation.voteOffset = add(vars.allocation.voteOffset, vars.deltaOffsetVotes);\n00779|             vars.allocation.vetoOffset = add(vars.allocation.vetoOffset, vars.deltaOffsetVetos);\n00780| \n00781|             // Update votes and vetos\n00782|             vars.allocation.voteLQTY = add(vars.allocation.voteLQTY, vars.deltaLQTYVotes);\n00783|             vars.allocation.vetoLQTY = add(vars.allocation.vetoLQTY, vars.deltaLQTYVetos);\n00784| \n00785|             vars.allocation.atEpoch = vars.currentEpoch;\n00786| \n00787|             // Voting power allocated to initiatives should never be negative, else it might break reward allocation\n00788|             // schemes such as `BribeInitiative` which distribute rewards in proportion to voting power allocated.\n00789|             assert(vars.allocation.voteLQTY * block.timestamp >= vars.allocation.voteOffset);\n00790|             assert(vars.allocation.vetoLQTY * block.timestamp >= vars.allocation.vetoOffset);\n00791| \n00792|             lqtyAllocatedByUserToInitiative[msg.sender][initiative] = vars.allocation;\n00793| \n00794|             // == USER STATE == //\n00795| \n00796|             // Remove from the user's unallocated LQTY and offset\n00797|             vars.userState.unallocatedLQTY =\n00798|                 sub(vars.userState.unallocatedLQTY, (vars.deltaLQTYVotes + vars.deltaLQTYVetos));\n00799|             vars.userState.unallocatedOffset =\n00800|                 sub(vars.userState.unallocatedOffset, (vars.deltaOffsetVotes + vars.deltaOffsetVetos));\n00801| \n00802|             // Add to the user's allocated LQTY and offset\n00803|             vars.userState.allocatedLQTY =\n00804|                 add(vars.userState.allocatedLQTY, (vars.deltaLQTYVotes + vars.deltaLQTYVetos));\n00805|             vars.userState.allocatedOffset =\n00806|                 add(vars.userState.allocatedOffset, (vars.deltaOffsetVotes + vars.deltaOffsetVetos));\n00807| \n00808|             HookStatus hookStatus;\n00809| \n00810|             // See https://github.com/liquity/V2-gov/issues/125\n00811|             // A malicious initiative could try to dissuade voters from casting vetos by consuming as much gas as\n00812|             // possible in the `onAfterAllocateLQTY` hook when detecting vetos.\n00813|             // We deem that the risks of calling into malicous initiatives upon veto allocation far outweigh the\n00814|             // benefits of notifying benevolent initiatives of vetos.\n00815|             if (vars.allocation.vetoLQTY == 0) {\n00816|                 // Replaces try / catch | Enforces sufficient gas is passed\n00817|                 hookStatus = safeCallWithMinGas(\n00818|                     initiative,\n00819|                     MIN_GAS_TO_HOOK,\n00820|                     0,\n00821|                     abi.encodeCall(\n00822|                         IInitiative.onAfterAllocateLQTY,\n00823|                         (vars.currentEpoch, msg.sender, vars.userState, vars.allocation, vars.initiativeState)\n00824|                     )\n00825|                 ) ? HookStatus.Succeeded : HookStatus.Failed;\n00826|             } else {\n00827|                 hookStatus = HookStatus.NotCalled;\n00828|             }\n00829| \n00830|             emit AllocateLQTY(\n00831|                 msg.sender, initiative, vars.deltaLQTYVotes, vars.deltaLQTYVetos, vars.currentEpoch, hookStatus\n00832|             );\n00833|         }\n00834| \n00835|         require(\n00836|             vars.userState.allocatedLQTY <= stakingV1.stakes(deriveUserProxyAddress(msg.sender)),\n00837|             \"Governance: insufficient-or-allocated-lqty\"\n00838|         );\n00839| \n00840|         globalState = vars.state;\n00841|         userStates[msg.sender] = vars.userState;\n00842|     }\n00843| \n00844|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00845|     function unregisterInitiative(address _initiative) external nonReentrant {\n00846|         /// Enforce FSM\n00847|         (VoteSnapshot memory votesSnapshot_, GlobalState memory state) = _snapshotVotes();\n00848|         (InitiativeVoteSnapshot memory votesForInitiativeSnapshot_, InitiativeState memory initiativeState) =\n00849|             _snapshotVotesForInitiative(_initiative);\n00850| \n00851|         (InitiativeStatus status,,) =\n00852|             getInitiativeState(_initiative, votesSnapshot_, votesForInitiativeSnapshot_, initiativeState);\n00853|         require(status == InitiativeStatus.UNREGISTERABLE, \"Governance: cannot-unregister-initiative\");\n00854| \n00855|         // Remove weight from current state\n00856|         uint256 currentEpoch = epoch();\n00857| \n00858|         // NOTE: Safe to remove | See `check_claim_soundness`\n00859|         assert(initiativeState.lastEpochClaim < currentEpoch - 1);\n00860| \n00861|         assert(state.countedVoteLQTY >= initiativeState.voteLQTY);\n00862|         assert(state.countedVoteOffset >= initiativeState.voteOffset);\n00863| \n00864|         state.countedVoteLQTY -= initiativeState.voteLQTY;\n00865|         state.countedVoteOffset -= initiativeState.voteOffset;\n00866| \n00867|         globalState = state;\n00868| \n00869|         /// Epoch will never reach 2^256 - 1\n00870|         registeredInitiatives[_initiative] = UNREGISTERED_INITIATIVE;\n00871| \n00872|         // Replaces try / catch | Enforces sufficient gas is passed\n00873|         bool success = safeCallWithMinGas(\n00874|             _initiative, MIN_GAS_TO_HOOK, 0, abi.encodeCall(IInitiative.onUnregisterInitiative, (currentEpoch))\n00875|         );\n00876| \n00877|         emit UnregisterInitiative(_initiative, currentEpoch, success ? HookStatus.Succeeded : HookStatus.Failed);\n00878|     }\n00879| \n00880|     /// @inheritdoc IGovernance\n00881|     function claimForInitiative(address _initiative) external nonReentrant returns (uint256) {\n00882|         // Accrue and update state\n00883|         (VoteSnapshot memory votesSnapshot_,) = _snapshotVotes();\n00884|         (InitiativeVoteSnapshot memory votesForInitiativeSnapshot_, InitiativeState memory initiativeState) =\n00885|             _snapshotVotesForInitiative(_initiative);\n00886| \n00887|         // Compute values on accrued state\n00888|         (InitiativeStatus status,, uint256 claimableAmount) =\n00889|             getInitiativeState(_initiative, votesSnapshot_, votesForInitiativeSnapshot_, initiativeState);\n00890| \n00891|         if (status != InitiativeStatus.CLAIMABLE) {\n00892|             return 0;\n00893|         }\n00894| \n00895|         /// INVARIANT: You can only claim for previous epoch\n00896|         assert(votesSnapshot_.forEpoch == epoch() - 1);\n00897| \n00898|         /// All unclaimed rewards are always recycled\n00899|         /// Invariant `lastEpochClaim` is < epoch() - 1; |\n00900|         /// If `lastEpochClaim` is older than epoch() - 1 it means the initiative couldn't claim any rewards this epoch\n00901|         initiativeStates[_initiative].lastEpochClaim = epoch() - 1;\n00902| \n00903|         /// INVARIANT, because of rounding errors the system can overpay\n00904|         /// We upscale the timestamp to reduce the impact of the loss\n00905|         /// However this is still possible\n00906|         uint256 available = bold.balanceOf(address(this));\n00907|         if (claimableAmount > available) {\n00908|             claimableAmount = available;\n00909|         }\n00910| \n00911|         bold.safeTransfer(_initiative, claimableAmount);\n00912| \n00913|         // Replaces try / catch | Enforces sufficient gas is passed\n00914|         bool success = safeCallWithMinGas(\n00915|             _initiative,\n00916|             MIN_GAS_TO_HOOK,\n00917|             0,\n00918|             abi.encodeCall(IInitiative.onClaimForInitiative, (votesSnapshot_.forEpoch, claimableAmount))\n00919|         );\n00920| \n00921|         emit ClaimForInitiative(\n00922|             _initiative, claimableAmount, votesSnapshot_.forEpoch, success ? HookStatus.Succeeded : HookStatus.Failed\n00923|         );\n00924| \n00925|         return claimableAmount;\n00926|     }\n00927| \n00928|     function _requireNoNOP(int256[] memory _absoluteLQTYVotes, int256[] memory _absoluteLQTYVetos) internal pure {\n00929|         for (uint256 i; i < _absoluteLQTYVotes.length; i++) {\n00930|             require(_absoluteLQTYVotes[i] > 0 || _absoluteLQTYVetos[i] > 0, \"Governance: voting nothing\");\n00931|         }\n00932|     }\n00933| \n00934|     function _requireNoSimultaneousVoteAndVeto(int256[] memory _absoluteLQTYVotes, int256[] memory _absoluteLQTYVetos)\n00935|         internal\n00936|         pure\n00937|     {\n00938|         for (uint256 i; i < _absoluteLQTYVotes.length; i++) {\n00939|             require(_absoluteLQTYVotes[i] == 0 || _absoluteLQTYVetos[i] == 0, \"Governance: vote-and-veto\");\n00940|         }\n00941|     }\n00942| }\n00943| \n\n(End of file - total 943 lines)\n</file>","title":"src/Governance.sol","metadata":{"preview":"// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity 0.8.24;\n\nimport {IERC20} from \"openzeppelin/contracts/interfaces/IERC20.sol\";\nimport {SafeERC20} from \"openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/utils/SafeERC20.sol\";\nimport {ReentrancyGuard} from \"openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol\";\n\nimport {IGovernance, UNREGISTERED_INITIATIVE} from \"./interfaces/IGovernance.sol\";\nimport {IInitiative} from \"./interfaces/IInitiative.sol\";\nimport {ILQTYStaking} from \"./interfaces/ILQTYStaking.sol\";\n\nimport {UserProxy} from \"./UserProxy.sol\";\nimport {UserProxyFactory} from \"./UserProxyFactory.sol\";\n\nimport {add, sub, max} from \"./utils/Math.sol\";\nimport {_requireNoDuplicates, _requireNoNegatives} from \"./utils/UniqueArray.sol\";\nimport {MultiDelegateCall} from \"./utils/MultiDelegateCall.sol\";\nimport {WAD, PermitParams} from \"./utils/Types.sol\";\nimport {safeCallWithMinGas} from \"./utils/SafeCallMinGas.sol\";\nimport {Ownable} from \"./utils/Ownable.sol\";"},"time":{"start":1763348531446,"end":1763348531447}}},{"id":"prt_a8fc359c4001olGvruGAgK0u5d","sessionID":"ses_5703d31c7ffeVgFwsdgMOLWFbj","messageID":"msg_a8fc34a78001vA7GEXslEy9dTI","type":"tool","callID":"call_ac16e8d0f7be4fe8a84c56e1","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/nelsonpereira/Documents/GitHub/Auditing/Fuzzing/Recon_Fuzzing/Liquity_V2_Gov/V2-gov/src/BribeInitiative.sol"},"output":"<file>\n00001| // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n00002| pragma solidity 0.8.24;\n00003| \n00004| import {IERC20} from \"openzeppelin/contracts/interfaces/IERC20.sol\";\n00005| import {SafeERC20} from \"openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/utils/SafeERC20.sol\";\n00006| \n00007| import {IGovernance, UNREGISTERED_INITIATIVE} from \"./interfaces/IGovernance.sol\";\n00008| import {IInitiative} from \"./interfaces/IInitiative.sol\";\n00009| import {IBribeInitiative} from \"./interfaces/IBribeInitiative.sol\";\n00010| \n00011| import {DoubleLinkedList} from \"./utils/DoubleLinkedList.sol\";\n00012| import {_lqtyToVotes} from \"./utils/VotingPower.sol\";\n00013| \n00014| contract BribeInitiative is IInitiative, IBribeInitiative {\n00015|     using SafeERC20 for IERC20;\n00016|     using DoubleLinkedList for DoubleLinkedList.List;\n00017| \n00018|     uint256 internal immutable EPOCH_START;\n00019|     uint256 internal immutable EPOCH_DURATION;\n00020| \n00021|     /// @inheritdoc IBribeInitiative\n00022|     IGovernance public immutable governance;\n00023|     /// @inheritdoc IBribeInitiative\n00024|     IERC20 public immutable bold;\n00025|     /// @inheritdoc IBribeInitiative\n00026|     IERC20 public immutable bribeToken;\n00027| \n00028|     /// @inheritdoc IBribeInitiative\n00029|     mapping(uint256 => Bribe) public bribeByEpoch;\n00030|     /// @inheritdoc IBribeInitiative\n00031|     mapping(address => mapping(uint256 => bool)) public claimedBribeAtEpoch;\n00032| \n00033|     /// Double linked list of the total LQTY allocated at a given epoch\n00034|     DoubleLinkedList.List internal totalLQTYAllocationByEpoch;\n00035|     /// Double linked list of LQTY allocated by a user at a given epoch\n00036|     mapping(address => DoubleLinkedList.List) internal lqtyAllocationByUserAtEpoch;\n00037| \n00038|     constructor(address _governance, address _bold, address _bribeToken) {\n00039|         require(_bribeToken != _bold, \"BribeInitiative: bribe-token-cannot-be-bold\");\n00040| \n00041|         governance = IGovernance(_governance);\n00042|         bold = IERC20(_bold);\n00043|         bribeToken = IERC20(_bribeToken);\n00044| \n00045|         EPOCH_START = governance.EPOCH_START();\n00046|         EPOCH_DURATION = governance.EPOCH_DURATION();\n00047|     }\n00048| \n00049|     modifier onlyGovernance() {\n00050|         require(msg.sender == address(governance), \"BribeInitiative: invalid-sender\");\n00051|         _;\n00052|     }\n00053| \n00054|     /// @inheritdoc IBribeInitiative\n00055|     function totalLQTYAllocatedByEpoch(uint256 _epoch) external view returns (uint256, uint256, uint256, uint256) {\n00056|         return (\n00057|             totalLQTYAllocationByEpoch.items[_epoch].lqty,\n00058|             totalLQTYAllocationByEpoch.items[_epoch].offset,\n00059|             totalLQTYAllocationByEpoch.items[_epoch].prev,\n00060|             totalLQTYAllocationByEpoch.items[_epoch].next\n00061|         );\n00062|     }\n00063| \n00064|     /// @inheritdoc IBribeInitiative\n00065|     function lqtyAllocatedByUserAtEpoch(address _user, uint256 _epoch)\n00066|         external\n00067|         view\n00068|         returns (uint256, uint256, uint256, uint256)\n00069|     {\n00070|         return (\n00071|             lqtyAllocationByUserAtEpoch[_user].items[_epoch].lqty,\n00072|             lqtyAllocationByUserAtEpoch[_user].items[_epoch].offset,\n00073|             lqtyAllocationByUserAtEpoch[_user].items[_epoch].prev,\n00074|             lqtyAllocationByUserAtEpoch[_user].items[_epoch].next\n00075|         );\n00076|     }\n00077| \n00078|     /// @inheritdoc IBribeInitiative\n00079|     function depositBribe(uint256 _boldAmount, uint256 _bribeTokenAmount, uint256 _epoch) external {\n00080|         uint256 epoch = governance.epoch();\n00081|         require(_epoch >= epoch, \"BribeInitiative: now-or-future-epochs\");\n00082| \n00083|         bribeByEpoch[_epoch].remainingBoldAmount += _boldAmount;\n00084|         bribeByEpoch[_epoch].remainingBribeTokenAmount += _bribeTokenAmount;\n00085| \n00086|         emit DepositBribe(msg.sender, _boldAmount, _bribeTokenAmount, _epoch);\n00087| \n00088|         bold.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), _boldAmount);\n00089|         bribeToken.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), _bribeTokenAmount);\n00090|     }\n00091| \n00092|     function _claimBribe(\n00093|         address _user,\n00094|         uint256 _epoch,\n00095|         uint256 _prevLQTYAllocationEpoch,\n00096|         uint256 _prevTotalLQTYAllocationEpoch\n00097|     ) internal returns (uint256 boldAmount, uint256 bribeTokenAmount) {\n00098|         require(_epoch < governance.epoch(), \"BribeInitiative: cannot-claim-for-current-epoch\");\n00099|         require(!claimedBribeAtEpoch[_user][_epoch], \"BribeInitiative: already-claimed\");\n00100| \n00101|         Bribe memory bribe = bribeByEpoch[_epoch];\n00102|         require(bribe.remainingBoldAmount != 0 || bribe.remainingBribeTokenAmount != 0, \"BribeInitiative: no-bribe\");\n00103| \n00104|         DoubleLinkedList.Item memory lqtyAllocation =\n00105|             lqtyAllocationByUserAtEpoch[_user].getItem(_prevLQTYAllocationEpoch);\n00106| \n00107|         require(\n00108|             _prevLQTYAllocationEpoch <= _epoch && (lqtyAllocation.next > _epoch || lqtyAllocation.next == 0),\n00109|             \"BribeInitiative: invalid-prev-lqty-allocation-epoch\"\n00110|         );\n00111|         DoubleLinkedList.Item memory totalLQTYAllocation =\n00112|             totalLQTYAllocationByEpoch.getItem(_prevTotalLQTYAllocationEpoch);\n00113|         require(\n00114|             _prevTotalLQTYAllocationEpoch <= _epoch\n00115|                 && (totalLQTYAllocation.next > _epoch || totalLQTYAllocation.next == 0),\n00116|             \"BribeInitiative: invalid-prev-total-lqty-allocation-epoch\"\n00117|         );\n00118| \n00119|         require(totalLQTYAllocation.lqty > 0, \"BribeInitiative: total-lqty-allocation-zero\");\n00120|         require(lqtyAllocation.lqty > 0, \"BribeInitiative: lqty-allocation-zero\");\n00121| \n00122|         // `Governance` guarantees that `votes` evaluates to 0 or greater for each initiative at the time of allocation.\n00123|         // Since the last possible moment to allocate within this epoch is 1 second before `epochEnd`, we have that:\n00124|         //  - `lqtyAllocation.lqty > 0` implies `votes > 0`\n00125|         //  - `totalLQTYAllocation.lqty > 0` implies `totalVotes > 0`\n00126| \n00127|         uint256 epochEnd = EPOCH_START + _epoch * EPOCH_DURATION;\n00128|         uint256 totalVotes = _lqtyToVotes(totalLQTYAllocation.lqty, epochEnd, totalLQTYAllocation.offset);\n00129|         uint256 votes = _lqtyToVotes(lqtyAllocation.lqty, epochEnd, lqtyAllocation.offset);\n00130|         uint256 remainingVotes = totalVotes - bribe.claimedVotes;\n00131| \n00132|         boldAmount = bribe.remainingBoldAmount * votes / remainingVotes;\n00133|         bribeTokenAmount = bribe.remainingBribeTokenAmount * votes / remainingVotes;\n00134|         bribe.remainingBoldAmount -= boldAmount;\n00135|         bribe.remainingBribeTokenAmount -= bribeTokenAmount;\n00136|         bribe.claimedVotes += votes;\n00137| \n00138|         bribeByEpoch[_epoch] = bribe;\n00139|         claimedBribeAtEpoch[_user][_epoch] = true;\n00140| \n00141|         emit ClaimBribe(_user, _epoch, boldAmount, bribeTokenAmount);\n00142|     }\n00143| \n00144|     /// @inheritdoc IBribeInitiative\n00145|     function claimBribes(ClaimData[] calldata _claimData)\n00146|         external\n00147|         returns (uint256 boldAmount, uint256 bribeTokenAmount)\n00148|     {\n00149|         for (uint256 i = 0; i < _claimData.length; i++) {\n00150|             ClaimData memory claimData = _claimData[i];\n00151|             (uint256 boldAmount_, uint256 bribeTokenAmount_) = _claimBribe(\n00152|                 msg.sender, claimData.epoch, claimData.prevLQTYAllocationEpoch, claimData.prevTotalLQTYAllocationEpoch\n00153|             );\n00154|             boldAmount += boldAmount_;\n00155|             bribeTokenAmount += bribeTokenAmount_;\n00156|         }\n00157| \n00158|         if (boldAmount != 0) bold.safeTransfer(msg.sender, boldAmount);\n00159|         if (bribeTokenAmount != 0) bribeToken.safeTransfer(msg.sender, bribeTokenAmount);\n00160|     }\n00161| \n00162|     /// @inheritdoc IInitiative\n00163|     function onRegisterInitiative(uint256) external virtual override onlyGovernance {}\n00164| \n00165|     /// @inheritdoc IInitiative\n00166|     function onUnregisterInitiative(uint256) external virtual override onlyGovernance {}\n00167| \n00168|     function _setTotalLQTYAllocationByEpoch(uint256 _epoch, uint256 _lqty, uint256 _offset, bool _insert) private {\n00169|         if (_insert) {\n00170|             totalLQTYAllocationByEpoch.insert(_epoch, _lqty, _offset, 0);\n00171|         } else {\n00172|             totalLQTYAllocationByEpoch.items[_epoch].lqty = _lqty;\n00173|             totalLQTYAllocationByEpoch.items[_epoch].offset = _offset;\n00174|         }\n00175|         emit ModifyTotalLQTYAllocation(_epoch, _lqty, _offset);\n00176|     }\n00177| \n00178|     function _setLQTYAllocationByUserAtEpoch(\n00179|         address _user,\n00180|         uint256 _epoch,\n00181|         uint256 _lqty,\n00182|         uint256 _offset,\n00183|         bool _insert\n00184|     ) private {\n00185|         if (_insert) {\n00186|             lqtyAllocationByUserAtEpoch[_user].insert(_epoch, _lqty, _offset, 0);\n00187|         } else {\n00188|             lqtyAllocationByUserAtEpoch[_user].items[_epoch].lqty = _lqty;\n00189|             lqtyAllocationByUserAtEpoch[_user].items[_epoch].offset = _offset;\n00190|         }\n00191|         emit ModifyLQTYAllocation(_user, _epoch, _lqty, _offset);\n00192|     }\n00193| \n00194|     /// @inheritdoc IBribeInitiative\n00195|     function getMostRecentUserEpoch(address _user) external view returns (uint256) {\n00196|         uint256 mostRecentUserEpoch = lqtyAllocationByUserAtEpoch[_user].getHead();\n00197| \n00198|         return mostRecentUserEpoch;\n00199|     }\n00200| \n00201|     /// @inheritdoc IBribeInitiative\n00202|     function getMostRecentTotalEpoch() external view returns (uint256) {\n00203|         uint256 mostRecentTotalEpoch = totalLQTYAllocationByEpoch.getHead();\n00204| \n00205|         return mostRecentTotalEpoch;\n00206|     }\n00207| \n00208|     function onAfterAllocateLQTY(\n00209|         uint256 _currentEpoch,\n00210|         address _user,\n00211|         IGovernance.UserState calldata,\n00212|         IGovernance.Allocation calldata _allocation,\n00213|         IGovernance.InitiativeState calldata _initiativeState\n00214|     ) external virtual onlyGovernance {\n00215|         uint256 mostRecentUserEpoch = lqtyAllocationByUserAtEpoch[_user].getHead();\n00216|         uint256 mostRecentTotalEpoch = totalLQTYAllocationByEpoch.getHead();\n00217| \n00218|         _setTotalLQTYAllocationByEpoch(\n00219|             _currentEpoch,\n00220|             _initiativeState.voteLQTY,\n00221|             _initiativeState.voteOffset,\n00222|             mostRecentTotalEpoch != _currentEpoch // Insert if current > recent\n00223|         );\n00224| \n00225|         _setLQTYAllocationByUserAtEpoch(\n00226|             _user,\n00227|             _currentEpoch,\n00228|             _allocation.voteLQTY,\n00229|             _allocation.voteOffset,\n00230|             mostRecentUserEpoch != _currentEpoch // Insert if user current > recent\n00231|         );\n00232|     }\n00233| \n00234|     /// @inheritdoc IInitiative\n00235|     function onClaimForInitiative(uint256, uint256) external virtual override onlyGovernance {}\n00236| }\n00237| \n\n(End of file - total 237 lines)\n</file>","title":"src/BribeInitiative.sol","metadata":{"preview":"// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity 0.8.24;\n\nimport {IERC20} from \"openzeppelin/contracts/interfaces/IERC20.sol\";\nimport {SafeERC20} from \"openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/utils/SafeERC20.sol\";\n\nimport {IGovernance, UNREGISTERED_INITIATIVE} from \"./interfaces/IGovernance.sol\";\nimport {IInitiative} from \"./interfaces/IInitiative.sol\";\nimport {IBribeInitiative} from \"./interfaces/IBribeInitiative.sol\";\n\nimport {DoubleLinkedList} from \"./utils/DoubleLinkedList.sol\";\nimport {_lqtyToVotes} from \"./utils/VotingPower.sol\";\n\ncontract BribeInitiative is IInitiative, IBribeInitiative {\n    using SafeERC20 for IERC20;\n    using DoubleLinkedList for DoubleLinkedList.List;\n\n    uint256 internal immutable EPOCH_START;\n    uint256 internal immutable EPOCH_DURATION;\n"},"time":{"start":1763348535752,"end":1763348535755}}},{"id":"prt_a8fc368f50019NA5zYgjpQ5FzW","sessionID":"ses_5703d31c7ffeVgFwsdgMOLWFbj","messageID":"msg_a8fc35b4e001w7z0S09Vi3vmjh","type":"tool","callID":"call_abc3800e703a4314b04eb3bd","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/nelsonpereira/Documents/GitHub/Auditing/Fuzzing/Recon_Fuzzing/Liquity_V2_Gov/V2-gov/test/recon/Setup.sol"},"output":"<file>\n00001| // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0\n00002| pragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n00003| \n00004| // Chimera deps\n00005| import {BaseSetup} from \"@chimera/BaseSetup.sol\";\n00006| import {vm} from \"@chimera/Hevm.sol\";\n00007| \n00008| // Managers\n00009| import {ActorManager} from \"@recon/ActorManager.sol\";\n00010| import {AssetManager} from \"@recon/AssetManager.sol\";\n00011| \n00012| // Helpers\n00013| import {Utils} from \"@recon/Utils.sol\";\n00014| \n00015| // Your deps\n00016| import \"src/BribeInitiative.sol\";\n00017| import \"src/Governance.sol\";\n00018| import {IGovernance} from \"src/interfaces/IGovernance.sol\";\n00019| import {IERC20} from \"openzeppelin/contracts/interfaces/IERC20.sol\";\n00020| \n00021| // Mocks\n00022| import {MockERC20Tester} from \"../mocks/MockERC20Tester.sol\";\n00023| import {MockStakingV1} from \"../mocks/MockStakingV1.sol\";\n00024| \n00025| abstract contract Setup is BaseSetup, ActorManager, AssetManager, Utils {\n00026|     // Configuration constants\n00027|     uint256 internal constant DECIMALS = 18;\n00028| \n00029|     // Core contracts\n00030|     BribeInitiative bribeInitiative;\n00031|     Governance governance;\n00032| \n00033|     // Token contracts\n00034|     MockERC20Tester lqty;\n00035|     MockERC20Tester lusd;\n00036|     MockERC20Tester bold;\n00037|     MockERC20Tester bribeToken;\n00038| \n00039|     // Infrastructure contracts\n00040|     MockStakingV1 stakingV1;\n00041| \n00042|     /// === Setup === ///\n00043|     /// This contains all calls to be performed in the tester constructor, both for Echidna and Foundry\n00044|     function setup() internal virtual override {\n00045|         // 1. Add actors\n00046|         _addActor(address(0x100)); // Actor 1\n00047|         _addActor(address(0x200)); // Actor 2\n00048| \n00049|         // 2. Deploy tokens\n00050|         lqty = new MockERC20Tester(\"Liquity\", \"LQTY\");\n00051|         lusd = new MockERC20Tester(\"Liquity USD\", \"LUSD\");\n00052|         bold = new MockERC20Tester(\"BOLD Stablecoin\", \"BOLD\");\n00053|         bribeToken = new MockERC20Tester(\"Bribe Token\", \"BRYB\");\n00054| \n00055|         // 3. Deploy MockStakingV1\n00056|         stakingV1 = new MockStakingV1(lqty, lusd);\n00057| \n00058|         // Set wildcard spender for stakingV1 (like in real LQTYStaking)\n00059|         lqty.mock_setWildcardSpender(address(stakingV1), true);\n00060| \n00061|         // 4. Create governance configuration\n00062|         // CONFIGURABLE: These parameters can be modified via governance functions\n00063|         IGovernance.Configuration memory config = IGovernance.Configuration({\n00064|             registrationFee: 1e18,\n00065|             registrationThresholdFactor: 0.01e18,\n00066|             unregistrationThresholdFactor: 4e18,\n00067|             unregistrationAfterEpochs: 4,\n00068|             votingThresholdFactor: 0.04e18,\n00069|             minClaim: 500e18,\n00070|             minAccrual: 1000e18,\n00071|             epochStart: block.timestamp - (604800 * 3), // 3 weeks ago (to enable registration)\n00072|             epochDuration: 604800, // 1 week\n00073|             epochVotingCutoff: 518400 // 6 days\n00074|         });\n00075| \n00076|         // 5. Deploy governance\n00077|         address[] memory initialInitiatives = new address[](0);\n00078|         governance = new Governance(\n00079|             address(lqty),\n00080|             address(lusd),\n00081|             address(stakingV1),\n00082|             address(bold),\n00083|             config,\n00084|             address(this),\n00085|             initialInitiatives\n00086|         );\n00087| \n00088|         // 6. Deploy bribe initiative\n00089|         bribeInitiative = new BribeInitiative(\n00090|             address(governance),\n00091|             address(bold),\n00092|             address(bribeToken)\n00093|         );\n00094| \n00095|         // 7. Mint tokens to actors manually (MockERC20Tester has onlyOwner on mint)\n00096|         address[] memory actors = _getActors();\n00097|         uint256 mintAmount = type(uint88).max;\n00098| \n00099|         for (uint256 i = 0; i < actors.length; i++) {\n00100|             lqty.mint(actors[i], mintAmount);\n00101|             lusd.mint(actors[i], mintAmount);\n00102|             bold.mint(actors[i], mintAmount);\n00103|             bribeToken.mint(actors[i], mintAmount);\n00104|         }\n00105| \n00106|         // 8. Set up approvals for each actor to all relevant contracts\n00107|         // We need to approve: governance, bribeInitiative, stakingV1, and each actor's userProxy\n00108|         for (uint256 i = 0; i < actors.length; i++) {\n00109|             address userProxy = governance.deriveUserProxyAddress(actors[i]);\n00110| \n00111|             address[] memory approvalArray = new address[](4);\n00112|             approvalArray[0] = address(governance);\n00113|             approvalArray[1] = address(bribeInitiative);\n00114|             approvalArray[2] = address(stakingV1);\n00115|             approvalArray[3] = userProxy;\n00116| \n00117|             for (uint256 j = 0; j < approvalArray.length; j++) {\n00118|                 vm.prank(actors[i]);\n00119|                 lqty.approve(approvalArray[j], type(uint256).max);\n00120|                 vm.prank(actors[i]);\n00121|                 lusd.approve(approvalArray[j], type(uint256).max);\n00122|                 vm.prank(actors[i]);\n00123|                 bold.approve(approvalArray[j], type(uint256).max);\n00124|                 vm.prank(actors[i]);\n00125|                 bribeToken.approve(approvalArray[j], type(uint256).max);\n00126|             }\n00127|         }\n00128| \n00129|         // 9. Add custom tokens to asset manager\n00130|         _addAsset(address(lqty));\n00131|         _addAsset(address(lusd));\n00132|         _addAsset(address(bold));\n00133|         _addAsset(address(bribeToken));\n00134|     }\n00135| \n00136|     /// === MODIFIERS === ///\n00137|     /// Prank admin and actor\n00138| \n00139|     modifier asAdmin {\n00140|         vm.prank(address(this));\n00141|         _;\n00142|     }\n00143| \n00144|     modifier asActor {\n00145|         vm.prank(address(_getActor()));\n00146|         _;\n00147|     }\n00148| }\n00149| \n\n(End of file - total 149 lines)\n</file>","title":"test/recon/Setup.sol","metadata":{"preview":"// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\n// Chimera deps\nimport {BaseSetup} from \"@chimera/BaseSetup.sol\";\nimport {vm} from \"@chimera/Hevm.sol\";\n\n// Managers\nimport {ActorManager} from \"@recon/ActorManager.sol\";\nimport {AssetManager} from \"@recon/AssetManager.sol\";\n\n// Helpers\nimport {Utils} from \"@recon/Utils.sol\";\n\n// Your deps\nimport \"src/BribeInitiative.sol\";\nimport \"src/Governance.sol\";\nimport {IGovernance} from \"src/interfaces/IGovernance.sol\";\nimport {IERC20} from \"openzeppelin/contracts/interfaces/IERC20.sol\";\n"},"time":{"start":1763348539640,"end":1763348539643}}},{"id":"prt_a8fc376a3001WL4gl7ghYUb9mA","sessionID":"ses_5703d31c7ffeVgFwsdgMOLWFbj","messageID":"msg_a8fc36a08001PU1riMsAGoATc7","type":"tool","callID":"call_4d94129a6cf846f1bb52c2e9","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/nelsonpereira/Documents/GitHub/Auditing/Fuzzing/Recon_Fuzzing/Liquity_V2_Gov/V2-gov/test/recon/TargetFunctions.sol"},"output":"<file>\n00001| // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0\n00002| pragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n00003| \n00004| // Chimera deps\n00005| import {vm} from \"@chimera/Hevm.sol\";\n00006| \n00007| // Helpers\n00008| import {Panic} from \"@recon/Panic.sol\";\n00009| \n00010| // Targets\n00011| // NOTE: Always import and apply them in alphabetical order, so much easier to debug!\n00012| import { AdminTargets } from \"./targets/AdminTargets.sol\";\n00013| import { BribeInitiativeTargets } from \"./targets/BribeInitiativeTargets.sol\";\n00014| import { DoomsdayTargets } from \"./targets/DoomsdayTargets.sol\";\n00015| import { GovernanceTargets } from \"./targets/GovernanceTargets.sol\";\n00016| import { ManagersTargets } from \"./targets/ManagersTargets.sol\";\n00017| \n00018| abstract contract TargetFunctions is\n00019|     AdminTargets,\n00020|     BribeInitiativeTargets,\n00021|     DoomsdayTargets,\n00022|     GovernanceTargets,\n00023|     ManagersTargets\n00024| {\n00025|     /// CUSTOM TARGET FUNCTIONS - Add your own target functions here ///\n00026| \n00027| \n00028|     /// AUTO GENERATED TARGET FUNCTIONS - WARNING: DO NOT DELETE OR MODIFY THIS LINE ///\n00029| }\n00030| \n\n(End of file - total 30 lines)\n</file>","title":"test/recon/TargetFunctions.sol","metadata":{"preview":"// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\n// Chimera deps\nimport {vm} from \"@chimera/Hevm.sol\";\n\n// Helpers\nimport {Panic} from \"@recon/Panic.sol\";\n\n// Targets\n// NOTE: Always import and apply them in alphabetical order, so much easier to debug!\nimport { AdminTargets } from \"./targets/AdminTargets.sol\";\nimport { BribeInitiativeTargets } from \"./targets/BribeInitiativeTargets.sol\";\nimport { DoomsdayTargets } from \"./targets/DoomsdayTargets.sol\";\nimport { GovernanceTargets } from \"./targets/GovernanceTargets.sol\";\nimport { ManagersTargets } from \"./targets/ManagersTargets.sol\";\n\nabstract contract TargetFunctions is\n    AdminTargets,\n    BribeInitiativeTargets,"},"time":{"start":1763348543142,"end":1763348543145}}},{"id":"prt_a8fc38bff0015O2C74rfnuIoY7","sessionID":"ses_5703d31c7ffeVgFwsdgMOLWFbj","messageID":"msg_a8fc3785c001aYtZ8yP44uWP4x","type":"tool","callID":"call_09103c50bf364db89535b65c","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/nelsonpereira/Documents/GitHub/Auditing/Fuzzing/Recon_Fuzzing/Liquity_V2_Gov/V2-gov/test/recon/targets/GovernanceTargets.sol"},"output":"<file>\n00001| // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0\n00002| pragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n00003| \n00004| import {BaseTargetFunctions} from \"@chimera/BaseTargetFunctions.sol\";\n00005| import {BeforeAfter} from \"../BeforeAfter.sol\";\n00006| import {Properties} from \"../Properties.sol\";\n00007| // Chimera deps\n00008| import {vm} from \"@chimera/Hevm.sol\";\n00009| \n00010| // Helpers\n00011| import {Panic} from \"@recon/Panic.sol\";\n00012| \n00013| import \"src/Governance.sol\";\n00014| \n00015| abstract contract GovernanceTargets is\n00016|     BaseTargetFunctions,\n00017|     Properties\n00018| {\n00019|     /// CUSTOM TARGET FUNCTIONS - Add your own target functions here ///\n00020| \n00021| \n00022|     /// AUTO GENERATED TARGET FUNCTIONS - WARNING: DO NOT DELETE OR MODIFY THIS LINE ///\n00023| \n00024|     function governance_allocateLQTY(address[] memory _initiativesToReset, address[] memory _initiatives, int256[] memory _absoluteLQTYVotes, int256[] memory _absoluteLQTYVetos) public asActor {\n00025|         governance.allocateLQTY(_initiativesToReset, _initiatives, _absoluteLQTYVotes, _absoluteLQTYVetos);\n00026|     }\n00027| \n00028|     function governance_calculateVotingThreshold() public asActor {\n00029|         governance.calculateVotingThreshold();\n00030|     }\n00031| \n00032|     function governance_claimForInitiative(address _initiative) public asActor {\n00033|         governance.claimForInitiative(_initiative);\n00034|     }\n00035| \n00036|     function governance_claimFromStakingV1(address _rewardRecipient) public asActor {\n00037|         governance.claimFromStakingV1(_rewardRecipient);\n00038|     }\n00039| \n00040|     function governance_deployUserProxy() public asActor {\n00041|         governance.deployUserProxy();\n00042|     }\n00043| \n00044|     function governance_depositLQTY(uint256 _lqtyAmount) public asActor {\n00045|         governance.depositLQTY(_lqtyAmount);\n00046|     }\n00047| \n00048|     function governance_depositLQTY(uint256 _lqtyAmount, bool _doSendRewards, address _recipient) public asActor {\n00049|         governance.depositLQTY(_lqtyAmount, _doSendRewards, _recipient);\n00050|     }\n00051| \n00052|     function governance_depositLQTYViaPermit(uint256 _lqtyAmount, PermitParams memory _permitParams, bool _doSendRewards, address _recipient) public asActor {\n00053|         governance.depositLQTYViaPermit(_lqtyAmount, _permitParams, _doSendRewards, _recipient);\n00054|     }\n00055| \n00056|     function governance_depositLQTYViaPermit(uint256 _lqtyAmount, PermitParams memory _permitParams) public asActor {\n00057|         governance.depositLQTYViaPermit(_lqtyAmount, _permitParams);\n00058|     }\n00059| \n00060|     function governance_getInitiativeState(address _initiative) public asActor {\n00061|         governance.getInitiativeState(_initiative);\n00062|     }\n00063| \n00064|     function governance_multiDelegateCall(bytes[] memory inputs) public asActor {\n00065|         governance.multiDelegateCall(inputs);\n00066|     }\n00067| \n00068|     function governance_registerInitiative(address _initiative) public asActor {\n00069|         governance.registerInitiative(_initiative);\n00070|     }\n00071| \n00072|     function governance_resetAllocations(address[] memory _initiativesToReset, bool checkAll) public asActor {\n00073|         governance.resetAllocations(_initiativesToReset, checkAll);\n00074|     }\n00075| \n00076|     function governance_snapshotVotesForInitiative(address _initiative) public asActor {\n00077|         governance.snapshotVotesForInitiative(_initiative);\n00078|     }\n00079| \n00080|     function governance_unregisterInitiative(address _initiative) public asActor {\n00081|         governance.unregisterInitiative(_initiative);\n00082|     }\n00083| \n00084|     function governance_withdrawLQTY(uint256 _lqtyAmount) public asActor {\n00085|         governance.withdrawLQTY(_lqtyAmount);\n00086|     }\n00087| \n00088|     function governance_withdrawLQTY(uint256 _lqtyAmount, bool _doSendRewards, address _recipient) public asActor {\n00089|         governance.withdrawLQTY(_lqtyAmount, _doSendRewards, _recipient);\n00090|     }\n00091| }\n\n(End of file - total 91 lines)\n</file>","title":"test/recon/targets/GovernanceTargets.sol","metadata":{"preview":"// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {BaseTargetFunctions} from \"@chimera/BaseTargetFunctions.sol\";\nimport {BeforeAfter} from \"../BeforeAfter.sol\";\nimport {Properties} from \"../Properties.sol\";\n// Chimera deps\nimport {vm} from \"@chimera/Hevm.sol\";\n\n// Helpers\nimport {Panic} from \"@recon/Panic.sol\";\n\nimport \"src/Governance.sol\";\n\nabstract contract GovernanceTargets is\n    BaseTargetFunctions,\n    Properties\n{\n    /// CUSTOM TARGET FUNCTIONS - Add your own target functions here ///\n"},"time":{"start":1763348548611,"end":1763348548614}}},{"id":"prt_a8fc39978001fNiBIR0FJHsHi5","sessionID":"ses_5703d31c7ffeVgFwsdgMOLWFbj","messageID":"msg_a8fc38d6d001QBNkurNDFATE4a","type":"tool","callID":"call_f85ca37619f44af9a31801a2","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/nelsonpereira/Documents/GitHub/Auditing/Fuzzing/Recon_Fuzzing/Liquity_V2_Gov/V2-gov/test/recon/targets/BribeInitiativeTargets.sol"},"output":"<file>\n00001| // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0\n00002| pragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n00003| \n00004| import {BaseTargetFunctions} from \"@chimera/BaseTargetFunctions.sol\";\n00005| import {BeforeAfter} from \"../BeforeAfter.sol\";\n00006| import {Properties} from \"../Properties.sol\";\n00007| // Chimera deps\n00008| import {vm} from \"@chimera/Hevm.sol\";\n00009| \n00010| // Helpers\n00011| import {Panic} from \"@recon/Panic.sol\";\n00012| \n00013| import \"src/BribeInitiative.sol\";\n00014| \n00015| abstract contract BribeInitiativeTargets is\n00016|     BaseTargetFunctions,\n00017|     Properties\n00018| {\n00019|     /// CUSTOM TARGET FUNCTIONS - Add your own target functions here ///\n00020| \n00021| \n00022|     /// AUTO GENERATED TARGET FUNCTIONS - WARNING: DO NOT DELETE OR MODIFY THIS LINE ///\n00023| \n00024|     function bribeInitiative_claimBribes(IBribeInitiative.ClaimData[] memory _claimData) public asActor {\n00025|         bribeInitiative.claimBribes(_claimData);\n00026|     }\n00027| \n00028|     function bribeInitiative_depositBribe(uint256 _boldAmount, uint256 _bribeTokenAmount, uint256 _epoch) public asActor {\n00029|         bribeInitiative.depositBribe(_boldAmount, _bribeTokenAmount, _epoch);\n00030|     }\n00031| \n00032|     function bribeInitiative_onAfterAllocateLQTY(uint256 _currentEpoch, address _user, IGovernance.UserState memory _userState, IGovernance.Allocation memory _allocation, IGovernance.InitiativeState memory _initiativeState) public asActor {\n00033|         bribeInitiative.onAfterAllocateLQTY(_currentEpoch, _user, _userState, _allocation, _initiativeState);\n00034|     }\n00035| \n00036|     function bribeInitiative_onClaimForInitiative(uint256 , uint256 ) public asActor {\n00037|         bribeInitiative.onClaimForInitiative(0, 0);\n00038|     }\n00039| \n00040|     function bribeInitiative_onRegisterInitiative(uint256 ) public asActor {\n00041|         bribeInitiative.onRegisterInitiative(0);\n00042|     }\n00043| \n00044|     function bribeInitiative_onUnregisterInitiative(uint256 ) public asActor {\n00045|         bribeInitiative.onUnregisterInitiative(0);\n00046|     }\n00047| }\n\n(End of file - total 47 lines)\n</file>","title":"test/recon/targets/BribeInitiativeTargets.sol","metadata":{"preview":"// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {BaseTargetFunctions} from \"@chimera/BaseTargetFunctions.sol\";\nimport {BeforeAfter} from \"../BeforeAfter.sol\";\nimport {Properties} from \"../Properties.sol\";\n// Chimera deps\nimport {vm} from \"@chimera/Hevm.sol\";\n\n// Helpers\nimport {Panic} from \"@recon/Panic.sol\";\n\nimport \"src/BribeInitiative.sol\";\n\nabstract contract BribeInitiativeTargets is\n    BaseTargetFunctions,\n    Properties\n{\n    /// CUSTOM TARGET FUNCTIONS - Add your own target functions here ///\n"},"time":{"start":1763348552060,"end":1763348552063}}},{"id":"prt_a8fc3b067001PwhLJ7NXjb2MdR","sessionID":"ses_5703d31c7ffeVgFwsdgMOLWFbj","messageID":"msg_a8fc39a9b001dxeGVQ3yFBvAHD","type":"tool","callID":"call_0c55be85251f406995be6390","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/nelsonpereira/Documents/GitHub/Auditing/Fuzzing/Recon_Fuzzing/Liquity_V2_Gov/V2-gov/src/utils/Types.sol"},"output":"<file>\n00001| // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n00002| pragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n00003| \n00004| struct PermitParams {\n00005|     address owner;\n00006|     address spender;\n00007|     uint256 value;\n00008|     uint256 deadline;\n00009|     uint8 v;\n00010|     bytes32 r;\n00011|     bytes32 s;\n00012| }\n00013| \n00014| uint256 constant WAD = 1e18;\n00015| \n\n(End of file - total 15 lines)\n</file>","title":"src/utils/Types.sol","metadata":{"preview":"// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\nstruct PermitParams {\n    address owner;\n    address spender;\n    uint256 value;\n    uint256 deadline;\n    uint8 v;\n    bytes32 r;\n    bytes32 s;\n}\n\nuint256 constant WAD = 1e18;\n"},"time":{"start":1763348557928,"end":1763348557930}}},{"id":"prt_a8fc3c25a001CTDCxvN8RGly5n","sessionID":"ses_5703d31c7ffeVgFwsdgMOLWFbj","messageID":"msg_a8fc3b19a001w0t6360KiMdRg8","type":"tool","callID":"call_419721aa29f442f6bef69e98","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/nelsonpereira/Documents/GitHub/Auditing/Fuzzing/Recon_Fuzzing/Liquity_V2_Gov/V2-gov/src/interfaces/IBribeInitiative.sol"},"output":"<file>\n00001| // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n00002| pragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n00003| \n00004| import {IERC20} from \"openzeppelin/contracts/interfaces/IERC20.sol\";\n00005| \n00006| import {IGovernance} from \"./IGovernance.sol\";\n00007| \n00008| interface IBribeInitiative {\n00009|     event DepositBribe(address depositor, uint256 boldAmount, uint256 bribeTokenAmount, uint256 epoch);\n00010|     event ModifyLQTYAllocation(address user, uint256 epoch, uint256 lqtyAllocated, uint256 offset);\n00011|     event ModifyTotalLQTYAllocation(uint256 epoch, uint256 totalLQTYAllocated, uint256 offset);\n00012|     event ClaimBribe(address user, uint256 epoch, uint256 boldAmount, uint256 bribeTokenAmount);\n00013| \n00014|     /// @notice Address of the governance contract\n00015|     /// @return governance Adress of the governance contract\n00016|     function governance() external view returns (IGovernance governance);\n00017|     /// @notice Address of the BOLD token\n00018|     /// @return bold Address of the BOLD token\n00019|     function bold() external view returns (IERC20 bold);\n00020|     /// @notice Address of the bribe token\n00021|     /// @return bribeToken Address of the bribe token\n00022|     function bribeToken() external view returns (IERC20 bribeToken);\n00023| \n00024|     struct Bribe {\n00025|         uint256 remainingBoldAmount;\n00026|         uint256 remainingBribeTokenAmount; // [scaled as 10 ** bribeToken.decimals()]\n00027|         uint256 claimedVotes;\n00028|     }\n00029| \n00030|     /// @notice Amount of bribe tokens deposited for a given epoch\n00031|     /// @param _epoch Epoch at which the bribe was deposited\n00032|     /// @return remainingBoldAmount Amount of BOLD tokens that haven't been claimed yet\n00033|     /// @return remainingBribeTokenAmount Amount of bribe tokens that haven't been claimed yet\n00034|     /// @return claimedVotes Sum of voting power of users who have already claimed their bribes\n00035|     function bribeByEpoch(uint256 _epoch)\n00036|         external\n00037|         view\n00038|         returns (uint256 remainingBoldAmount, uint256 remainingBribeTokenAmount, uint256 claimedVotes);\n00039|     /// @notice Check if a user has claimed bribes for a given epoch\n00040|     /// @param _user Address of the user\n00041|     /// @param _epoch Epoch at which the bribe may have been claimed by the user\n00042|     /// @return claimed If the user has claimed the bribe\n00043|     function claimedBribeAtEpoch(address _user, uint256 _epoch) external view returns (bool claimed);\n00044| \n00045|     /// @notice Total LQTY allocated to the initiative at a given epoch\n00046|     ///         Voting power can be calculated as `totalLQTYAllocated * timestamp - offset`\n00047|     /// @param _epoch Epoch at which the LQTY was allocated\n00048|     /// @return totalLQTYAllocated Total LQTY allocated\n00049|     /// @return offset Voting power offset\n00050|     /// @return prev Previous epoch at which the total LQTY allocation was updated\n00051|     /// @return next Next epoch at which the total LQTY allocation was updated\n00052|     function totalLQTYAllocatedByEpoch(uint256 _epoch)\n00053|         external\n00054|         view\n00055|         returns (uint256 totalLQTYAllocated, uint256 offset, uint256 prev, uint256 next);\n00056|     /// @notice LQTY allocated by a user to the initiative at a given epoch\n00057|     ///         Voting power can be calculated as `lqtyAllocated * timestamp - offset`\n00058|     /// @param _user Address of the user\n00059|     /// @param _epoch Epoch at which the LQTY was allocated by the user\n00060|     /// @return lqtyAllocated LQTY allocated by the user\n00061|     /// @return offset Voting power offset\n00062|     /// @return prev Previous epoch at which the user updated the LQTY allocation for this initiative\n00063|     /// @return next Next epoch at which the user updated the LQTY allocation for this initiative\n00064|     function lqtyAllocatedByUserAtEpoch(address _user, uint256 _epoch)\n00065|         external\n00066|         view\n00067|         returns (uint256 lqtyAllocated, uint256 offset, uint256 prev, uint256 next);\n00068| \n00069|     /// @notice Deposit bribe tokens for a given epoch\n00070|     /// @dev The caller has to approve this contract to spend the BOLD and bribe tokens.\n00071|     /// The caller can only deposit bribes for future epochs\n00072|     /// @param _boldAmount Amount of BOLD tokens to deposit\n00073|     /// @param _bribeTokenAmount Amount of bribe tokens to deposit\n00074|     /// @param _epoch Epoch at which the bribe is deposited\n00075|     function depositBribe(uint256 _boldAmount, uint256 _bribeTokenAmount, uint256 _epoch) external;\n00076| \n00077|     struct ClaimData {\n00078|         // Epoch at which the user wants to claim the bribes\n00079|         uint256 epoch;\n00080|         // Epoch at which the user updated the LQTY allocation for this initiative\n00081|         uint256 prevLQTYAllocationEpoch;\n00082|         // Epoch at which the total LQTY allocation is updated for this initiative\n00083|         uint256 prevTotalLQTYAllocationEpoch;\n00084|     }\n00085| \n00086|     /// @notice Claim bribes for a user\n00087|     /// @dev The user can only claim bribes for past epochs.\n00088|     /// The arrays `_epochs`, `_prevLQTYAllocationEpochs` and `_prevTotalLQTYAllocationEpochs` should be sorted\n00089|     /// from oldest epoch to the newest. The length of the arrays has to be the same.\n00090|     /// @param _claimData Array specifying the epochs at which the user wants to claim the bribes\n00091|     function claimBribes(ClaimData[] calldata _claimData)\n00092|         external\n00093|         returns (uint256 boldAmount, uint256 bribeTokenAmount);\n00094| \n00095|     /// @notice Given a user address return the last recorded epoch for their allocation\n00096|     function getMostRecentUserEpoch(address _user) external view returns (uint256);\n00097| \n00098|     /// @notice Return the last recorded epoch for the system\n00099|     function getMostRecentTotalEpoch() external view returns (uint256);\n00100| }\n00101| \n\n(End of file - total 101 lines)\n</file>","title":"src/interfaces/IBribeInitiative.sol","metadata":{"preview":"// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\nimport {IERC20} from \"openzeppelin/contracts/interfaces/IERC20.sol\";\n\nimport {IGovernance} from \"./IGovernance.sol\";\n\ninterface IBribeInitiative {\n    event DepositBribe(address depositor, uint256 boldAmount, uint256 bribeTokenAmount, uint256 epoch);\n    event ModifyLQTYAllocation(address user, uint256 epoch, uint256 lqtyAllocated, uint256 offset);\n    event ModifyTotalLQTYAllocation(uint256 epoch, uint256 totalLQTYAllocated, uint256 offset);\n    event ClaimBribe(address user, uint256 epoch, uint256 boldAmount, uint256 bribeTokenAmount);\n\n    /// @notice Address of the governance contract\n    /// @return governance Adress of the governance contract\n    function governance() external view returns (IGovernance governance);\n    /// @notice Address of the BOLD token\n    /// @return bold Address of the BOLD token\n    function bold() external view returns (IERC20 bold);\n    /// @notice Address of the bribe token"},"time":{"start":1763348562525,"end":1763348562529}}},{"id":"prt_a8fc3d638001vUi4VvFnZ1b40j","sessionID":"ses_5703d31c7ffeVgFwsdgMOLWFbj","messageID":"msg_a8fc3c3f0001FMrnF43bWSOI32","type":"tool","callID":"call_b50f06ff0e2c476c94921300","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/nelsonpereira/Documents/GitHub/Auditing/Fuzzing/Recon_Fuzzing/Liquity_V2_Gov/V2-gov/src/interfaces/IGovernance.sol","limit":100},"output":"<file>\n00001| // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n00002| pragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n00003| \n00004| import {IERC20} from \"openzeppelin/contracts/interfaces/IERC20.sol\";\n00005| \n00006| import {ILQTYStaking} from \"./ILQTYStaking.sol\";\n00007| \n00008| import {PermitParams} from \"../utils/Types.sol\";\n00009| \n00010| uint256 constant UNREGISTERED_INITIATIVE = type(uint256).max;\n00011| \n00012| interface IGovernance {\n00013|     enum HookStatus {\n00014|         Failed,\n00015|         Succeeded,\n00016|         NotCalled\n00017|     }\n00018| \n00019|     /// @notice Emitted when a user deposits LQTY\n00020|     /// @param user The account depositing LQTY\n00021|     /// @param rewardRecipient The account receiving the LUSD/ETH rewards earned from staking in V1, if claimed\n00022|     /// @param lqtyAmount The amount of LQTY being deposited\n00023|     /// @return lusdReceived Amount of LUSD tokens received as a side-effect of staking new LQTY\n00024|     /// @return lusdSent Amount of LUSD tokens sent to `rewardRecipient` (may include previously received LUSD)\n00025|     /// @return ethReceived Amount of ETH received as a side-effect of staking new LQTY\n00026|     /// @return ethSent Amount of ETH sent to `rewardRecipient` (may include previously received ETH)\n00027|     event DepositLQTY(\n00028|         address indexed user,\n00029|         address rewardRecipient,\n00030|         uint256 lqtyAmount,\n00031|         uint256 lusdReceived,\n00032|         uint256 lusdSent,\n00033|         uint256 ethReceived,\n00034|         uint256 ethSent\n00035|     );\n00036| \n00037|     /// @notice Emitted when a user withdraws LQTY or claims V1 staking rewards\n00038|     /// @param user The account withdrawing LQTY or claiming V1 staking rewards\n00039|     /// @param recipient The account receiving the LQTY withdrawn, and if claimed, the LUSD/ETH rewards earned from staking in V1\n00040|     /// @return lqtyReceived Amount of LQTY tokens actually withdrawn (may be lower than the `_lqtyAmount` passed to `withdrawLQTY`)\n00041|     /// @return lqtySent Amount of LQTY tokens sent to `recipient` (may include LQTY sent to the user's proxy from sources other than V1 staking)\n00042|     /// @return lusdReceived Amount of LUSD tokens received as a side-effect of staking new LQTY\n00043|     /// @return lusdSent Amount of LUSD tokens sent to `recipient` (may include previously received LUSD)\n00044|     /// @return ethReceived Amount of ETH received as a side-effect of staking new LQTY\n00045|     /// @return ethSent Amount of ETH sent to `recipient` (may include previously received ETH)\n00046|     event WithdrawLQTY(\n00047|         address indexed user,\n00048|         address recipient,\n00049|         uint256 lqtyReceived,\n00050|         uint256 lqtySent,\n00051|         uint256 lusdReceived,\n00052|         uint256 lusdSent,\n00053|         uint256 ethReceived,\n00054|         uint256 ethSent\n00055|     );\n00056| \n00057|     event SnapshotVotes(uint256 votes, uint256 forEpoch, uint256 boldAccrued);\n00058|     event SnapshotVotesForInitiative(address indexed initiative, uint256 votes, uint256 vetos, uint256 forEpoch);\n00059| \n00060|     event RegisterInitiative(address initiative, address registrant, uint256 atEpoch, HookStatus hookStatus);\n00061|     event UnregisterInitiative(address initiative, uint256 atEpoch, HookStatus hookStatus);\n00062| \n00063|     event AllocateLQTY(\n00064|         address indexed user,\n00065|         address indexed initiative,\n00066|         int256 deltaVoteLQTY,\n00067|         int256 deltaVetoLQTY,\n00068|         uint256 atEpoch,\n00069|         HookStatus hookStatus\n00070|     );\n00071|     event ClaimForInitiative(address indexed initiative, uint256 bold, uint256 forEpoch, HookStatus hookStatus);\n00072| \n00073|     struct Configuration {\n00074|         uint256 registrationFee;\n00075|         uint256 registrationThresholdFactor;\n00076|         uint256 unregistrationThresholdFactor;\n00077|         uint256 unregistrationAfterEpochs;\n00078|         uint256 votingThresholdFactor;\n00079|         uint256 minClaim;\n00080|         uint256 minAccrual;\n00081|         uint256 epochStart;\n00082|         uint256 epochDuration;\n00083|         uint256 epochVotingCutoff;\n00084|     }\n00085| \n00086|     function registerInitialInitiatives(address[] memory _initiatives) external;\n00087| \n00088|     /// @notice Address of the LQTY StakingV1 contract\n00089|     /// @return stakingV1 Address of the LQTY StakingV1 contract\n00090|     function stakingV1() external view returns (ILQTYStaking stakingV1);\n00091|     /// @notice Address of the LQTY token\n00092|     /// @return lqty Address of the LQTY token\n00093|     function lqty() external view returns (IERC20 lqty);\n00094|     /// @notice Address of the BOLD token\n00095|     /// @return bold Address of the BOLD token\n00096|     function bold() external view returns (IERC20 bold);\n00097|     /// @notice Timestamp at which the first epoch starts\n00098|     /// @return epochStart Timestamp at which the first epoch starts\n00099|     function EPOCH_START() external view returns (uint256 epochStart);\n00100|     /// @notice Duration of an epoch in seconds (e.g. 1 week)\n\n(File has more lines. Use 'offset' parameter to read beyond line 100)\n</file>","title":"src/interfaces/IGovernance.sol","metadata":{"preview":"// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\nimport {IERC20} from \"openzeppelin/contracts/interfaces/IERC20.sol\";\n\nimport {ILQTYStaking} from \"./ILQTYStaking.sol\";\n\nimport {PermitParams} from \"../utils/Types.sol\";\n\nuint256 constant UNREGISTERED_INITIATIVE = type(uint256).max;\n\ninterface IGovernance {\n    enum HookStatus {\n        Failed,\n        Succeeded,\n        NotCalled\n    }\n\n    /// @notice Emitted when a user deposits LQTY\n    /// @param user The account depositing LQTY"},"time":{"start":1763348567610,"end":1763348567614}}},{"id":"prt_a8fc3f692001ZyI4f1GGLayC8m","sessionID":"ses_5703d31c7ffeVgFwsdgMOLWFbj","messageID":"msg_a8fc3d79a001YdtBoH8RVbwt7d","type":"tool","callID":"call_ab2d6fa8fb664eb4b9913a4a","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/nelsonpereira/Documents/GitHub/Auditing/Fuzzing/Recon_Fuzzing/Liquity_V2_Gov/V2-gov/src/interfaces/IGovernance.sol","limit":100,"offset":100},"output":"<file>\n00101|     /// @return epochDuration Epoch duration\n00102|     function EPOCH_DURATION() external view returns (uint256 epochDuration);\n00103|     /// @notice Voting period of an epoch in seconds (e.g. 6 days)\n00104|     /// @return epochVotingCutoff Epoch voting cutoff\n00105|     function EPOCH_VOTING_CUTOFF() external view returns (uint256 epochVotingCutoff);\n00106|     /// @notice Minimum BOLD amount that has to be claimed, if an initiative doesn't have enough votes to meet the\n00107|     /// criteria then it's votes a excluded from the vote count and distribution\n00108|     /// @return minClaim Minimum claim amount\n00109|     function MIN_CLAIM() external view returns (uint256 minClaim);\n00110|     /// @notice Minimum amount of BOLD that have to be accrued for an epoch, otherwise accrual will be skipped for\n00111|     /// that epoch\n00112|     /// @return minAccrual Minimum amount of BOLD\n00113|     function MIN_ACCRUAL() external view returns (uint256 minAccrual);\n00114|     /// @notice Amount of BOLD to be paid in order to register a new initiative\n00115|     /// @return registrationFee Registration fee\n00116|     function REGISTRATION_FEE() external view returns (uint256 registrationFee);\n00117|     /// @notice Share of all votes that are necessary to register a new initiative\n00118|     /// @return registrationThresholdFactor Threshold factor\n00119|     function REGISTRATION_THRESHOLD_FACTOR() external view returns (uint256 registrationThresholdFactor);\n00120|     /// @notice Multiple of the voting threshold in vetos that are necessary to unregister an initiative\n00121|     /// @return unregistrationThresholdFactor Unregistration threshold factor\n00122|     function UNREGISTRATION_THRESHOLD_FACTOR() external view returns (uint256 unregistrationThresholdFactor);\n00123|     /// @notice Number of epochs an initiative has to be inactive before it can be unregistered\n00124|     /// @return unregistrationAfterEpochs Number of epochs\n00125|     function UNREGISTRATION_AFTER_EPOCHS() external view returns (uint256 unregistrationAfterEpochs);\n00126|     /// @notice Share of all votes that are necessary for an initiative to be included in the vote count\n00127|     /// @return votingThresholdFactor Voting threshold factor\n00128|     function VOTING_THRESHOLD_FACTOR() external view returns (uint256 votingThresholdFactor);\n00129| \n00130|     /// @notice Returns the amount of BOLD accrued since last epoch (last snapshot)\n00131|     /// @return boldAccrued BOLD accrued\n00132|     function boldAccrued() external view returns (uint256 boldAccrued);\n00133| \n00134|     struct VoteSnapshot {\n00135|         uint256 votes; // Votes at epoch transition\n00136|         uint256 forEpoch; // Epoch for which the votes are counted\n00137|     }\n00138| \n00139|     struct InitiativeVoteSnapshot {\n00140|         uint256 votes; // Votes at epoch transition\n00141|         uint256 forEpoch; // Epoch for which the votes are counted\n00142|         uint256 lastCountedEpoch; // Epoch at which which the votes where counted last in the global snapshot\n00143|         uint256 vetos; // Vetos at epoch transition\n00144|     }\n00145| \n00146|     /// @notice Returns the vote count snapshot of the previous epoch\n00147|     /// @return votes Number of votes\n00148|     /// @return forEpoch Epoch for which the votes are counted\n00149|     function votesSnapshot() external view returns (uint256 votes, uint256 forEpoch);\n00150|     /// @notice Returns the vote count snapshot for an initiative of the previous epoch\n00151|     /// @param _initiative Address of the initiative\n00152|     /// @return votes Number of votes\n00153|     /// @return forEpoch Epoch for which the votes are counted\n00154|     /// @return lastCountedEpoch Epoch at which which the votes where counted last in the global snapshot\n00155|     function votesForInitiativeSnapshot(address _initiative)\n00156|         external\n00157|         view\n00158|         returns (uint256 votes, uint256 forEpoch, uint256 lastCountedEpoch, uint256 vetos);\n00159| \n00160|     struct Allocation {\n00161|         uint256 voteLQTY; // LQTY allocated vouching for the initiative\n00162|         uint256 voteOffset; // Offset associated with LQTY vouching for the initiative\n00163|         uint256 vetoLQTY; // LQTY vetoing the initiative\n00164|         uint256 vetoOffset; // Offset associated with LQTY vetoing the initiative\n00165|         uint256 atEpoch; // Epoch at which the allocation was last updated\n00166|     }\n00167| \n00168|     struct UserState {\n00169|         uint256 unallocatedLQTY; // LQTY deposited and unallocated\n00170|         uint256 unallocatedOffset; // The offset sum corresponding to the unallocated LQTY\n00171|         uint256 allocatedLQTY; // LQTY allocated by the user to initatives\n00172|         uint256 allocatedOffset; // The offset sum corresponding to the allocated LQTY\n00173|     }\n00174| \n00175|     struct InitiativeState {\n00176|         uint256 voteLQTY; // LQTY allocated vouching for the initiative\n00177|         uint256 voteOffset; // Offset associated with LQTY vouching for to the initative\n00178|         uint256 vetoLQTY; // LQTY allocated vetoing the initiative\n00179|         uint256 vetoOffset; // Offset associated with LQTY veoting the initative\n00180|         uint256 lastEpochClaim;\n00181|     }\n00182| \n00183|     struct GlobalState {\n00184|         uint256 countedVoteLQTY; // Total LQTY that is included in vote counting\n00185|         uint256 countedVoteOffset; // Offset associated with the counted vote LQTY\n00186|     }\n00187| \n00188|     /// @notice Returns the user's state\n00189|     /// @return unallocatedLQTY LQTY deposited and unallocated\n00190|     /// @return unallocatedOffset Offset associated with unallocated LQTY\n00191|     /// @return allocatedLQTY allocated by the user to initatives\n00192|     /// @return allocatedOffset Offset associated with allocated LQTY\n00193|     function userStates(address _user)\n00194|         external\n00195|         view\n00196|         returns (uint256 unallocatedLQTY, uint256 unallocatedOffset, uint256 allocatedLQTY, uint256 allocatedOffset);\n00197|     /// @notice Returns the initiative's state\n00198|     /// @param _initiative Address of the initiative\n00199|     /// @return voteLQTY LQTY allocated vouching for the initiative\n00200|     /// @return voteOffset Offset associated with voteLQTY\n\n(File has more lines. Use 'offset' parameter to read beyond line 200)\n</file>","title":"src/interfaces/IGovernance.sol","metadata":{"preview":"    /// @return epochDuration Epoch duration\n    function EPOCH_DURATION() external view returns (uint256 epochDuration);\n    /// @notice Voting period of an epoch in seconds (e.g. 6 days)\n    /// @return epochVotingCutoff Epoch voting cutoff\n    function EPOCH_VOTING_CUTOFF() external view returns (uint256 epochVotingCutoff);\n  